{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4cb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07476-3862-7671-a25f-75740245e24f"},"sequence":192,"recorded_at":1780531400000379,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"6261e351-4998-4c04-80fc-b607e4fc4484"},"task_id":"6261e351-4998-4c04-80fc-b607e4fc4484","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"6261e351-4998-4c04-80fc-b607e4fc4484","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2z3se0/TASK-260830-2z3se0_rework-evidence-rev3.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2z3se0 — round-3 rework evidence (answers review-verdict-rev2)\n2|\n3|Tree: worktree `task-board/story/STORY-260830-3drr2m`. Production changes in\n4|`internal/sessadapter/operations.go` (B1 only); all other changes are tests in\n5|`internal/sessadapter/` plus one LOGBOOK entry. No commit per the CR-shape\n6|instruction.\n7|\n8|## Fixes per finding\n9|\n10|### B1 (blocking) — archive-mode validate success refused unconditionally\n11|`checkValidateResult` no longer calls `checkValidateNullability`. The pinned\n12|§7.8 validate success member list names no target members, so the\n13|request-body nullability rule cannot apply to successes — option (a) from the\n14|verdict, resolved by the document, not by a product decision.\n15|`checkValidateNullability` and `checkValidateResult` comments updated to state\n16|the request-only scope. New `TestValidateSuccessAdmitsEveryMode` drives\n17|staged/live/archive successes through `CheckSuccessBody`; the archive subtest\n18|is the previously unreachable mode (904 tests green over it).\n19|\n20|### B2 (blocking) — four member maps without a content pin\n21|`TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec` now compares the Members gate map as\n22|a set against the derived list for all four tail bodies (success, failure,\n23|manifest, doctor). The `manifestMembers :=` local is renamed\n24|`derivedManifest` so it cannot shadow the production map. The log now reports\n25|member-map comparisons: `20 member maps pinned across 21 bodies`\n26|(SupportedContractVersions has no production gate map by design).\n27|\n28|### B3 (blocking) — constructor-closure sentence false for additive arms\n29|New `TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction` derives the denominator from\n30|production: every `axerror.New` site must sit inside a registered constructor\n31|body, and the registered set must equal the error-constructing vars exactly\n32|(both directions). The `refusalConstructors` comment now states what both\n33|gates do (census for new sites, alias gate for aliased uses).\n34|\n35|### N4 — CheckCallBinding zero-fact gates\n36|New `TestCheckCallBindingZeroFactsRefuse`: all five zero-fact exemptions\n37|refuse through their own arms (role, provider, manifest digest, executable\n38|digest, zero admitted tuple).\n39|\n40|### N5 — census sentences ahead of the walk\n41|`vocabularyTablesInFile` handles shared and paired multi-name initializers\n42|(three synthetic vectors added); the tagless-switch exemption is confined to\n43|`readUTF16Escape` by function name (`classifySwitch`, proven by\n44|`TestSwitchClassifierNamesItsExemption`); the census stated bound now names\n45|the five function-local obligation lists (pinned behaviourally in both\n46|directions) and the const/regexp shapes (absent from production).\n47|\n48|## Mutant battery (narrowing; 14 killed / 14)\n49|\n50|Method: each mutant applied by exact-string replacement, grep-confirmed\n51|PRESENT and `go vet`-clean before its verdict; production restored after\n52|every mutant (script `/tmp/mutant-battery-r3.py`). The named test passes on\n53|the clean tree in every row (checked by the harness).\n54|\n55|| Mutant | Narrows the gate to | Named test that fails |\n56||---|---|---|\n57|| M-B1 success nullability restored | refuse archive success with no target members | TestValidateSuccessAdmitsEveryMode |\n58|| M-B2a successMembers +1 | success envelope admits an extra member | TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec |\n59|| M-B2b failureMembers +1 | failure envelope admits an extra member | TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec |\n60|| M-B2c manifestMembers +1 | manifest admits an extra member | TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec |\n61|| M-B2d doctorResultMembers +1 | doctor result admits an extra member | TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec |\n62|| M-B3a 8th ctor failQuota + additive arm | unregistered constructor ships an unwitnessed arm | TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction |\n63|| M-B3b inline axerror.New + additive arm | bare axerror.New ships an unwitnessed arm | TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction |\n64|| M-N4a role gate `&& binding.Role != \"\"` | admit a call under a roleless binding | TestCheckCallBindingZeroFactsRefuse/zero_binding_role |\n65|| M-N4b provider gate `&& binding.ProviderID != \"\"` | admit a call under a providerless binding | TestCheckCallBindingZeroFactsRefuse/zero_binding_provider |\n66|| M-N4c manifest gate `&& binding.AdapterManifestDigest != \"\"` | admit a call under a digestless binding | TestCheckCallBindingZeroFactsRefuse/zero_binding_manifest_digest |\n67|| M-N4d executable gate `&& binding.ExecutableSHA256 != \"\"` | admit a call under an exeless binding | TestCheckCallBindingZeroFactsRefuse/zero_binding_executable_digest |\n68|| M-N4e tuple gate `&& admitted != (Tuple{})` | admit a call against a zero tuple | TestCheckCallBindingZeroFactsRefuse/zero_admitted_tuple |\n69|| M-N5a paired var table planted | paired table hides from the scan | TestClosedVocabularyTablesAreRegistered |\n70|| M-N5b tagless switch planted elsewhere | tagless switch outside readUTF16Escape hides | TestAllProductionSwitchesAreClassified |\n71|\n72|Survivors: none. No stated-bound exemptions were exercised by this battery.\n73|\n74|Anti-inflation check (the rev2 B3 lesson): with M-B3a / M-B3b applied, the\n75|FULL suite fails on exactly one test — `TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction`\n76|— while the 323-arm inventory stays green. The kill comes from the new\n77|census, not the count floor.\n78|\n79|Method bounds: battery is scoped to this rework (B1–B3, N4, N5). It does not\n80|re-traverse the rev2 93-site surface; rev2 kills were not re-measured here.\n81|Delegated packages (`canonicaljson`, `scalar`, `axerror`) not attacked. The\n82|package has no in-repo importers; gates are measured at its exported API.\n83|\n84|## AC coverage delta (this round; prior 10-row coverage stands)\n85|\n86|| AC row | Production call site | Named committed test |\n87||---|---|---|\n88|| closed operations, validate modes | CheckSuccessBody (operations.go) | TestValidateSuccessAdmitsEveryMode (staged/live/archive) |\n89|| negative/refusal, member gates | unknownMember via CheckSuccessEnvelope / DecodeManifest / DecodeDoctorResult | TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec (20 map pins) |\n90|| negative/refusal, construction closure | Discover / CheckSuccessBody | TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction |\n91|| tuple/binding gates | CheckCallBinding (discovery.go) | TestCheckCallBindingZeroFactsRefuse (5 of 5) |\n92|| census scope | scanVocabularyTables / switch walk | multi-name vectors, TestSwitchClassifierNamesItsExemption |\n93|\n94|## Gates (exit codes observed directly, no pipes)\n95|\n96|- `go build ./...`: exit 0\n97|- `go test ./... -count=1`: 17/17 packages ok, exit 0\n98|- `go test ./internal/sessadapter/ -count=1 -v`: 923 PASS, 0 FAIL, exit 0\n99|- `go test ./internal/sessadapter/ -cover`: 81.5% of statements, exit 0\n100|- `go test -race ./internal/sessadapter/ -count=1`: exit 0\n101|- `go vet ./...`: exit 0; `GOOS=windows go vet ./internal/sessadapter/`: exit 0\n102|- `gofmt -l internal/`: empty\n103|-