.2048][0..1024]\", \"warnings\")\n306|\t\tif err != nil {\n307|\t\t\treturn Probe{}, err\n308|\t\t}\n309|\t\treturn Probe{}, failure\n310|\t}\n311|\tif !checkExtensions(members[\"extensions\"]) {\n312|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe extensions are not reverse-DNS keyed\", \"extensions\")\n313|\t\tif err != nil {\n314|\t\t\treturn Probe{}, err\n315|\t\t}\n316|\t\treturn Probe{}, failure\n317|\t}\n318|\treturn Probe{\n319|\t\tProviderID:     providerID,\n320|\t\tManifestDigest: manifestDigest.String(),\n321|\t\tAdapterVersion: adapterVersion,\n322|\t\tEnvironment:    environment,\n323|\t\tCapabilities:   capabilities,\n324|\t\tWarnings:       warnings,\n325|\t}, nil\n326|}\n327|\n328|// decodeCapabilities validates the closed capability map: exactly\n329|// the fifteen registry names, each with a closed value. The map\n330|// carries no order — names are the keys — so omission and extra\n331|// are the two refused directions, and duplication is already\n332|// refused by the strict decode.\n333|func decodeCapabilities(raw json.RawMessage) (map[string]Capability, error) {\n334|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(bytesTrimSpace(raw))\n335|\tif fault != nil {\n336|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter capabilities \"+fault.detail, \"capabilities\")\n337|\t\tif err != nil {\n338|\t\t\treturn nil, err\n339|\t\t}\n340|\t\treturn nil, failure\n341|\t}\n342|\tif len(members) != len(capabilityOrder) {\n343|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter capabilities do not carry exactly fifteen entries\", \"capabilities\")\n344|\t\tif err != nil {\n345|\t\t\treturn nil, err\n346|\t\t}\n347|\t\treturn nil, failure\n348|\t}\n349|\tcapabilities := make(map[string]Capability, len(capabilityOrder))\n350|\tfor _, name := range capabilityOrder {\n351|\t\trawValue, present := members[name]\n352|\t\tif !present {\n353|\t\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter capabilities omit a registry capability\", name)\n354|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n355|\t\t\t\treturn nil, err\n356|\t\t\t}\n357|\t\t\treturn nil, failure\n358|\t\t}\n359|\t\tvalue, err := decodeCapabilityValue(rawValue, name)\n360|\t\tif err != nil {\n361|\t\t\treturn nil, err\n362|\t\t}\n363|\t\tcapabilities[name] = value\n364|\t}\n365|\treturn capabilities, nil\n366|}\n367|\n368|// ProbeHostFacts are the host-held values the probe must equal:\n369|// the provider identifier and candidate kind from the probe\n370|// request the host built, the manifest digest the host computed,\n371|// and the manifest the host verified. Nothing here comes from the\n372|// adapter.\n373|type ProbeHostFacts struct {\n374|\tExpectedProviderID string\n375|\tExpectedKind       CandidateKind\n376|\tManifestDigest     string\n377|\tManifest           Manifest\n378|}\n379|\n380|// CheckProbe enforces the Section 7.8 probe equalities: provider\n381|// ID, manifest digest, and adapter version equal the verified\n382|// manifest and host values, and the reported tuple is the\n383|// manifest's tuple — the adapter's one semantic native\n384|// environment, so a probe reporting any other tuple is an\n385|// unrequested tuple and is refused. The tuple's adapter version\n386|// must equal the probe's own adapter version: both name the same\n387|// probed software, and a probe disagreeing with itself is\n388|// refused. Whether the tuple's environment version satisfies the\n389|// manifest's version-range constraint language is a stated bound:\n390|// the range grammar has no evaluation rule in Section 7.8.\n391|func CheckProbe(probe Probe, facts ProbeHostFacts) error {\n392|\tif probe.ProviderID != facts.ExpectedProviderID {\n393|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe provider identifier does not match the requested provider\", \"provider_id\")\n394|\t\tif err != nil {\n395|\t\t\treturn err\n396|\t\t}\n397|\t\treturn failure\n398|\t}\n399|\tif probe.ProviderID != facts.Manifest.ProviderID {\n400|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe provider identifier does not match the verified manifest\", \"provider_id\")\n401|\t\tif err != nil {\n402|\t\t\treturn err\n403|\t\t}\n404|\t\treturn failure\n405|\t}\n406|\tif probe.ManifestDigest != facts.ManifestDigest {\n407|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe manifest digest does not match the host-computed digest\", \"adapter_manifest_digest\")\n408|\t\tif err != nil {\n409|\t\t\treturn err\n410|\t\t}\n411|\t\treturn failure\n412|\t}\n413|\tif probe.AdapterVersion != facts.Manifest.AdapterVersion {\n414|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe adapter version does not match the verified manifest\", \"adapter_version\")\n415|\t\tif err != nil {\n416|\t\t\treturn err\n417|\t\t}\n418|\t\treturn failure\n419|\t}\n420|\tif probe.Environment.EnvironmentID != facts.Manifest.EnvironmentID {\n421|\t\tfailure, err := failUnsupportedTuple(\"adapter probe reports a tuple outside the manifest environment\", probe.Environment.EnvironmentID)\n422|\t\tif err != nil {\n423|\t\t\treturn err\n424|\t\t}\n425|\t\treturn failure\n426|\t}\n427|\tif probe.Environment.AdapterVersion != probe.AdapterVersion {\n428|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe tuple adapter version does not match the probe adapter version\", \"environment\")\n429|\t\tif err != nil {\n430|\t\t\treturn err\n431|\t\t}\n432|\t\treturn failure\n433|\t}\n434|\treturn nil\n435|}\n436|\n437|// CheckProbeRequest binds the probe request the host built to the\n438|// trusted candidate: the expected provider identifier and\n439|// candidate kind must equal the candidate the host will invoke.\n440|// A request naming a different provider or kind would attest a\n441|// probe for a candidate the host never observed.\n442|func CheckProbeRequest(expectedProviderID string, expectedKind CandidateKind, candidate TrustedCandidate) error {\n443|\tif expectedProviderID != candidate.ProviderID {\n444|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"probe request provider identifier does not match the trusted candidate\", \"expected_provider_id\")\n445|\t\tif err != nil {\n446|\t\t\treturn err\n447|\t\t}\n448|\t\treturn failure\n449|\t}\n450|\tif expectedKind != candidate.Kind {\n451|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"probe request candidate kind does not match the trusted candidate\", \"expected_candidate_kind\")\n452|\t\tif err != nil {\n453|\t\t\treturn err\n454|\t\t}\n455|\t\treturn failure\n456|\t}\n457|\treturn nil\n458|}\n459|\n460|// CapabilityUsable reports whether the named capability is a usable\n461|// surface: present in the closed registry with status=available and\n462|// enabled=true. Conditional, unsupported, and unknown surfaces are\n463|// never usable, and neither is a name outside the registry.\n464|func CapabilityUsable(probe Probe, name string) bool {\n465|\tvalue, present := probe.Capabilities[name]\n466|\tif !present {\n467|\t\treturn false\n468|\t}\n469|\treturn value.Status == \"available\" && value.Enabled\n470|}\n471|\n472|// ProviderCapability is one provider-probe capability the\n473|// target-write gate reads: the provider's portable-store and\n474|// native-resume facts live in the provider probe, not the adapter\n475|// probe, so the caller projects exactly those two surfaces.\n476|type ProviderCapability struct {\n477|\tStatus  string\n478|\tEnabled bool\n479|}\n480|\n481|// CheckTargetWriteGates enforces the Section 7.8 target-write\n482|// conjunction: available canonical-write or official-import,\n483|// native-read-back, native-resume-plan, and workspace-binding on\n484|// the adapter side, plus provider portable-store and native-resume\n485|// on the provider side. Exact execution bindings, accepted\n486|// non-revoked tuple entries, and current fixture plus bounded\n487|// resume-smoke evidence are the caller's adjacent gates\n488|// (CheckBinding, CheckTupleAdmission, CheckDoctorResult): this\n489|// gate decides the capability conjunction only. --force,\n490|// experimental profiles, and environment-name-only matches cannot\n491|// bypass these gates: the function takes no bypass parameter, so a\n492|// caller cannot express one. Unknown sources may be archived only\n493|// after safe byte enumeration; unknown targets never write —\n494|// which this gate enforces by refusing every capability it cannot\n495|// see as available and enabled.\n496|func CheckTargetWriteGates(adapter map[string]Capability, provider map[string]ProviderCapability) error {\n497|\tif !capabilityMapUsable(adapter, \"canonical_write\") && !capabilityMapUsable(adapter, \"official_import\") {\n498|\t\tfailure, err := failCapability(\"target write has neither usable canonical-write nor official-import\", \"canonical_write|official_import\")\n499|\t\tif err != nil {\n500|\t\t\treturn err\n501|\t\t}\n502|\t\treturn failure\n503|\t}\n504|\tfor _, name := range []string{\"native_read_back\", \"native_resume_plan\", \"workspace_binding\"} {\n505|\t\tif !capabilityMapUsable(adapter, name) {\n506|\t\t\tfailure, err := failCapability(\"target write misses a usable adapter capability\", name)\n507|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n508|\t\t\t\treturn err\n509|\t\t\t}\n510|\t\t\treturn failure\n511|\t\t}\n512|\t}\n513|\tfor _, name := range []string{\"portable_store\", \"native_resume\"} {\n514|\t\tvalue, present := provider[name]\n515|\t\tif !present || value.Status != \"available\" || !value.Enabled {\n516|\t\t\tfailure, err := failCapability(\"target write misses a usable provider capability\", \"provider:\"+name)\n517|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n518|\t\t\t\treturn err\n519|\t\t\t}\n520|\t\t\treturn failure\n521|\t\t}\n522|\t}\n523|\treturn nil\n524|}\n525|\n526|// capabilityMapUsable reports whether the named adapter capability\n527|// is usable. An absent name is not usable: the map must be the\n528|// decoded probe map, which always carries all fifteen.\n529|func capabilityMapUsable(adapter map[string]Capability, name string) bool {\n530|\tvalue, present := adapter[name]\n531|\tif !present {\n532|\t\treturn false\n533|\t}\n534|\treturn value.Status == \"available\" && value.Enabled\n535|}\n536|\n537|// doctorResultMembers is the exact doctor success-body member set.\n538|var doctorResultMembers = map[string]bool{\n539|\t\"context\":               true,\n540|\t\"direction\":             true,\n541|\t\"registry_sequence\":     true,\n542|\t\"registry_entry_status\": true,\n543|\t\"findings\":              true,\n544|\t\"healthy\":               true,\n545|\t\"extensions\":            true,\n546|}\n547|\n548|// doctorResultRequired lists doctorResultMembers in order.\n549|var doctorResultRequired = []string{\n550|\t\"context\",\n551|\t\"direction\",\n552|\t\"registry_sequence\",\n553|\t\"registry_entry_status\",\n554|\t\"findings\",\n555|\t\"healthy\",\n556|\t\"extensions\",\n557|}\n558|\n559|// DoctorResult is one validated doctor success body.\n560|type DoctorResult struct {\n561|\tContext          CallContext\n562|\tDirection        Direction\n563|\tRegistrySequence uint64\n564|\tEntryStatus      string\n565|\tFindings         []Finding\n566|\tHealthy          bool\n567|}\n568|\n569|// DecodeDoctorResult validates one closed doctor success body: the\n570|// echoed context, the direction in the closed vocabulary, the\n571|// registry sequence as uint53, the entry status in\n572|// accepted|revoked|absent, the findings, and the health flag. The\n573|// health rule itself is CheckDoctorHealthy: decoding proves shape,\n574|// not health.\n575|func DecodeDoctorResult(body []byte, sent CallContext, sentDirection Direction) (DoctorResult, error) {\n576|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(body)\n577|\tif fault != nil {\n578|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result \"+fault.detail, fault.member)\n579|\t\tif err != nil {\n580|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n581|\t\t}\n582|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n583|\t}\n584|\tif name, unknown := unknownMember(members, doctorResultMembers); unknown {\n585|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result carries unknown member\", name)\n586|\t\tif err != nil {\n587|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n588|\t\t}\n589|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n590|\t}\n591|\tif name, missing := missingMember(members, doctorResultRequired); missing {\n592|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result misses a required member\", name)\n593|\t\tif err != nil {\n594|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n595|\t\t}\n596|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n597|\t}\n598|\tcontext, err := CheckContextEcho(sent, members[\"context\"])\n599|\tif err != nil {\n600|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n601|\t}\n602|\tdirection, ok := rawString(members[\"direction\"])\n603|\tif !ok || !validDirection(direction) {\n604|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result direction is outside source_read|target_write\", \"direction\")\n605|\t\tif err != nil {\n606|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n607|\t\t}\n608|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n609|\t}\n610|\tif Direction(direction) != sentDirection {\n611|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result direction does not answer the request direction\", \"direction\")\n612|\t\tif err != nil {\n613|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n614|\t\t}\n615|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n616|\t}\n617|\tsequence, ok := checkUint53Bounds(members[\"registry_sequence\"], 0, maxUint53)\n618|\tif !ok {\n619|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result registry sequence is not a uint53\", \"registry_sequence\")\n620|\t\tif err != nil {\n621|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n622|\t\t}\n623|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n624|\t}\n625|\tstatus, ok := rawString(members[\"registry_entry_status\"])\n626|\tif !ok || !validRegistryEntryStatus(status) {\n627|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result entry status is outside accepted|revoked|absent\", \"registry_entry_status\")\n628|\t\tif err != nil {\n629|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n630|\t\t}\n631|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n632|\t}\n633|\tfindings, err := DecodeFindings(members[\"findings\"], 4096)\n634|\tif err != nil {\n635|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n636|\t}\n637|\thealthy, ok := rawBool(members[\"healthy\"])\n638|\tif !ok {\n639|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result health flag is not a boolean\", \"healthy\")\n640|\t\tif err != nil {\n641|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n642|\t\t}\n643|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n644|\t}\n645|\tif !checkExtensions(members[\"extensions\"]) {\n646|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result extensions are not reverse-DNS keyed\", \"extensions\")\n647|\t\tif err != nil {\n648|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n649|\t\t}\n650|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n651|\t}\n652|\treturn DoctorResult{\n653|\t\tContext:          context,\n654|\t\tDirection:        Direction(direction),\n655|\t\tRegistrySequence: sequence,\n656|\t\tEntryStatus:      status,\n657|\t\tFindings:         findings,\n658|\t\tHealthy:          healthy,\n659|\t}, nil\n660|}\n661|\n662|// CheckDoctorHealthy enforces the doctor health rule: healthy\n663|// requires an accepted exact binding and every required\n664|// capability. A healthy=true result over a revoked or absent entry\n665|// is refused, and so is a healthy=true result with any required\n666|// capability unusable. healthy=false is always structurally\n667|// admissible: the rule states necessary conditions, not\n668|// sufficient ones. Every required name must belong to the closed\n669|// fifteen-registry; a required set naming anything else is a\n670|// caller error, because the host cannot demand a surface the\n671|// contract never defined.\n672|func CheckDoctorHealthy(result DoctorResult, probe Probe, required []string) error {\n673|\tfor _, name := range required {\n674|\t\tif !validCapabilityName(name) {\n675|\t\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"doctor required set names a capability outside the closed registry\", \"required\")\n676|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n677|\t\t\t\treturn err\n678|\t\t\t}\n679|\t\t\treturn failure\n680|\t\t}\n681|\t}\n682|\tif !result.Healthy {\n683|\t\treturn nil\n684|\t}\n685|\tif result.EntryStatus != \"accepted\" {\n686|\t\tfailure, err := failCapability(\"doctor reports healthy without an accepted registry entry\", \"tuple_registry\")\n687|\t\tif err != nil {\n688|\t\t\treturn err\n689|\t\t}\n690|\t\treturn failure\n691|\t}\n692|\tfor _, name := range required {\n693|\t\tif !CapabilityUsable(probe, name) {\n694|\t\t\tfailure, err := failCapability(\"doctor reports healthy without a usable required capability\", name)\n695|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n696|\t\t\t\treturn err\n697|\t\t\t}\n698|\t\t\treturn failure\n699|\t\t}\n700|\t}\n701|\treturn nil\n702|}\n703|\n704|// validCapabilityName reports whether the name belongs to the\n705|// fifteen-capability registry.\n706|func validCapabilityName(name string) bool {\n707|\tfor _, capability := range capabilityOrder {\n708|\t\tif capability == name {\n709|\t\t\treturn true\n710|\t\t}\n711|\t}\n712|\treturn false\n713|}\n714|\n715|// DoctorRequiredCapabilities returns the closed required-capability\n716|// set for one doctor direction. For target_write it is the Section\n717|// 7.8 target-write adapter set: the import strategy selects which\n718|// member of the canonical-write/official-import pair is required,\n719|// and native-read-back, native-resume-plan, and workspace-binding\n720|// are always required. For source_read it is empty: Section 7.8\n721|// names no per-direction source set, so the caller carries its\n722|// tuple-registry-derived requirements explicitly rather than\n723|// reading them from an invented list. The strategy-to-pair mapping\n724|// is an interpretation recorded here, not a derived rule: the\n725|// target_official_import strategy authorizes the official-import\n726|// member, every other target strategy the canonical-write member.\n727|func DoctorRequiredCapabilities(direction Direction, useOfficialImport bool) []string {\n728|\tif direction != DirectionTargetWrite {\n729|\t\treturn nil\n730|\t}\n731|\twriter := \"canonical_write\"\n732|\tif useOfficialImport {\n733|\t\twriter = \"official_import\"\n734|\t}\n735|\treturn []string{writer, \"native_read_back\", \"native_resume_plan\", \"workspace_binding\"}\n736|}"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c55f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07476-3862-7671-a25f-75740245e24f"},"sequence":266,"recorded_at":1780531400000527,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"db8b6eb1-b398-4c47-aa68-47e2af1c4a31"},"task_id":"db8b6eb1-b398-4c47-aa68-47e2af1c4a31","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"db8b6eb1-b398-4c47-aa68-47e2af1c4a31"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c561","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07476-3862-7671-a25f-75740245e24f"},"sequence":267,"recorded_at":1780531400000529,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a"},"call_id":"call_01a07476c93579238b22f827158d1eb6","text":"Read text file `internal/sessadapter/probe.go`.\n1|package sessadapter\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"encoding/json\"\n5|)\n6|\n7|// This file validates the Section 7.8 Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0,\n8|// the capability-value rules, the probe equality gates against the\n9|// verified manifest and host values, the doctor health gate, and\n10|// the target-write capability gates.\n11|\n12|// probeSchema is the exact schema identifier the probe carries.\n13|const probeSchema = \"urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-probe\"\n14|\n15|// probeSchemaVersion is the only probe version this host accepts.\n16|const probeSchemaVersion = \"1.0.0\"\n17|\n18|// probeMembers is the exact Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0 member set:\n19|// schema, schema_version, provider_id, adapter_manifest_digest,\n20|// adapter_version, environment, capabilities, warnings, and\n21|// extensions.\n22|var probeMembers = map[string]bool{\n23|\t\"schema\":                  true,\n24|\t\"schema_version\":          true,\n25|\t\"provider_id\":             true,\n26|\t\"adapter_manifest_digest\": true,\n27|\t\"adapter_version\":         true,\n28|\t\"environment\":             true,\n29|\t\"capabilities\":            true,\n30|\t\"warnings\":                true,\n31|\t\"extensions\":              true,\n32|}\n33|\n34|// probeRequired lists probeMembers in a fixed order.\n35|var probeRequired = []string{\n36|\t\"schema\",\n37|\t\"schema_version\",\n38|\t\"provider_id\",\n39|\t\"adapter_manifest_digest\",\n40|\t\"adapter_version\",\n41|\t\"environment\",\n42|\t\"capabilities\",\n43|\t\"warnings\",\n44|\t\"extensions\",\n45|}\n46|\n47|// capabilityValueMembers is the exact per-capability value member\n48|// set: status, enabled, evidence, and detail. Only\n49|// status=available permits enabled=true.\n50|var capabilityValueMembers = map[string]bool{\n51|\t\"status\":   true,\n52|\t\"enabled\":  true,\n53|\t\"evidence\": true,\n54|\t\"detail\":   true,\n55|}\n56|\n57|// capabilityValueRequired lists capabilityValueMembers in order.\n58|var capabilityValueRequired = []string{\n59|\t\"status\",\n60|\t\"enabled\",\n61|\t\"evidence\",\n62|\t\"detail\",\n63|}\n64|\n65|// Capability is one validated capability value.\n66|type Capability struct {\n67|\tStatus   string\n68|\tEnabled  bool\n69|\tEvidence string\n70|\tDetail   string\n71|}\n72|\n73|// Probe is one validated Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0.\n74|type Probe struct {\n75|\tProviderID     string\n76|\tManifestDigest string\n77|\tAdapterVersion string\n78|\tEnvironment    Tuple\n79|\tCapabilities   map[string]Capability\n80|\tWarnings       []string\n81|}\n82|\n83|// decodeCapabilityValue validates one closed capability value:\n84|// status in available|conditional|unsupported|unknown, evidence in\n85|// the seven-vocabulary, detail as string[0..2048], and the\n86|// coherence rule that only available permits enabled=true. A\n87|// conditional, unsupported, or unknown capability with\n88|// enabled=true is a contradictory fact and invalidates the whole\n89|// probe, never a usable surface.\n90|func decodeCapabilityValue(raw json.RawMessage, name string) (Capability, error) {\n91|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(bytesTrimSpace(raw))\n92|\tif fault != nil {\n93|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter capability \"+fault.detail, name)\n94|\t\tif err != nil {\n95|\t\t\treturn Capability{}, err\n96|\t\t}\n97|\t\treturn Capability{}, failure\n98|\t}\n99|\tif member, unknown := unknownMember(members, capabilityValueMembers); unknown {\n100|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter capability value carries unknown member\", member)\n101|\t\tif err != nil {\n102|\t\t\treturn Capability{}, err\n103|\t\t}\n104|\t\treturn Capability{}, failure\n105|\t}\n106|\tif member, missing := missingMember(members, capabilityValueRequired); missing {\n107|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter capability value misses a required member\", member)\n108|\t\tif err != nil {\n109|\t\t\treturn Capability{}, err\n110|\t\t}\n111|\t\treturn Capability{}, failure\n112|\t}\n113|\tstatus, ok := rawString(members[\"status\"])\n114|\tif !ok || !validCapabilityStatus(status) {\n115|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter capability status is outside available|conditional|unsupported|unknown\", name)\n116|\t\tif err != nil {\n117|\t\t\treturn Capability{}, err\n118|\t\t}\n119|\t\treturn Capability{}, failure\n120|\t}\n121|\tenabled, ok := rawBool(members[\"enabled\"])\n122|\tif !ok {\n123|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter capability enabled flag is not a boolean\", name)\n124|\t\tif err != nil {\n125|\t\t\treturn Capability{}, err\n126|\t\t}\n127|\t\treturn Capability{}, failure\n128|\t}\n129|\tif enabled && status != \"available\" {\n130|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter capability is enabled without available status\", name)\n131|\t\tif err != nil {\n132|\t\t\treturn Capability{}, err\n133|\t\t}\n134|\t\treturn Capability{}, failure\n135|\t}\n136|\tevidence, ok := rawString(members[\"evidence\"])\n137|\tif !ok || !validCapabilityEvidence(evidence) {\n138|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter capability evidence is outside the seven-evidence vocabulary\", name)\n139|\t\tif err != nil {\n140|\t\t\treturn Capability{}, err\n141|\t\t}\n142|\t\treturn Capability{}, failure\n143|\t}\n144|\tdetail, ok := checkStringBounds(members[\"detail\"], 0, 2048)\n145|\tif !ok {\n146|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter capability detail is not a string[0..2048]\", name)\n147|\t\tif err != nil {\n148|\t\t\treturn Capability{}, err\n149|\t\t}\n150|\t\treturn Capability{}, failure\n151|\t}\n152|\treturn Capability{\n153|\t\tStatus:   status,\n154|\t\tEnabled:  enabled,\n155|\t\tEvidence: evidence,\n156|\t\tDetail:   detail,\n157|\t}, nil\n158|}\n159|\n160|// capabilityEvidences is the seven-evidence vocabulary Section 7.8\n161|// states. Membership is a table loop so the census derives it like\n162|// every other closed vocabulary.\n163|var capabilityEvidences = []string{\n164|\t\"documented\",\n165|\t\"probed\",\n166|\t\"accepted_test\",\n167|\t\"provider_contract\",\n168|\t\"inferred\",\n169|\t\"acceptance_required\",\n170|\t\"none\",\n171|}\n172|\n173|// validCapabilityEvidence reports whether the evidence token is one\n174|// of the seven Section 7.8 values.\n175|func validCapabilityEvidence(evidence string) bool {\n176|\tfor _, allowed := range capabilityEvidences {\n177|\t\tif evidence == allowed {\n178|\t\t\treturn true\n179|\t\t}\n180|\t}\n181|\treturn false\n182|}\n183|\n184|// capabilityStatuses is the four-status vocabulary Section 7.8\n185|// states. Membership is a table loop so the census derives it like\n186|// every other closed vocabulary.\n187|var capabilityStatuses = []string{\n188|\t\"available\",\n189|\t\"conditional\",\n190|\t\"unsupported\",\n191|\t\"unknown\",\n192|}\n193|\n194|// validCapabilityStatus reports whether the status token is one of\n195|// the four Section 7.8 values.\n196|func validCapabilityStatus(status string) bool {\n197|\tfor _, allowed := range capabilityStatuses {\n198|\t\tif status == allowed {\n199|\t\t\treturn true\n200|\t\t}\n201|\t}\n202|\treturn false\n203|}\n204|\n205|// registryEntryStatuses is the three-status doctor vocabulary the\n206|// Section 7.8 doctor row states: accepted, revoked, and absent.\n207|// Membership is a table loop so the census derives it like every\n208|// other closed vocabulary.\n209|var registryEntryStatuses = []string{\n210|\t\"accepted\",\n211|\t\"revoked\",\n212|\t\"absent\",\n213|}\n214|\n215|// validRegistryEntryStatus reports whether the status is one of\n216|// the three Section 7.8 doctor entry statuses.\n217|func validRegistryEntryStatus(status string) bool {\n218|\tfor _, allowed := range registryEntryStatuses {\n219|\t\tif status == allowed {\n220|\t\t\treturn true\n221|\t\t}\n222|\t}\n223|\treturn false\n224|}\n225|\n226|// DecodeProbe validates one probe-operation success body as the\n227|// closed Section 7.8 Session Adapter Probe: the exact members, all\n228|// fifteen capabilities with no omission and no extra, and the\n229|// value rules above. Missing, extra, duplicated, malformed, or\n230|// contradictory facts invalidate the whole probe and never mean\n231|// unsupported. Equality against the manifest and host values is\n232|// the separate CheckProbe gate: decoding proves shape, not\n233|// binding.\n234|func DecodeProbe(body []byte) (Probe, error) {\n235|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(body)\n236|\tif fault != nil {\n237|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe \"+fault.detail, fault.member)\n238|\t\tif err != nil {\n239|\t\t\treturn Probe{}, err\n240|\t\t}\n241|\t\treturn Probe{}, failure\n242|\t}\n243|\tif name, unknown := unknownMember(members, probeMembers); unknown {\n244|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe carries unknown member\", name)\n245|\t\tif err != nil {\n246|\t\t\treturn Probe{}, err\n247|\t\t}\n248|\t\treturn Probe{}, failure\n249|\t}\n250|\tif name, missing := missingMember(members, probeRequired); missing {\n251|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe misses a required member\", name)\n252|\t\tif err != nil {\n253|\t\t\treturn Probe{}, err\n254|\t\t}\n255|\t\treturn Probe{}, failure\n256|\t}\n257|\tif schema, ok := rawString(members[\"schema\"]); !ok || schema != probeSchema {\n258|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe schema is not the session adapter probe\", \"schema\")\n259|\t\tif err != nil {\n260|\t\t\treturn Probe{}, err\n261|\t\t}\n262|\t\treturn Probe{}, failure\n263|\t}\n264|\tif version, ok := rawString(members[\"schema_version\"]); !ok || version != probeSchemaVersion {\n265|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe version is not 1.0.0\", \"schema_version\")\n266|\t\tif err != nil {\n267|\t\t\treturn Probe{}, err\n268|\t\t}\n269|\t\treturn Probe{}, failure\n270|\t}\n271|\tproviderID, ok := rawString(members[\"provider_id\"])\n272|\tif !ok || !providerIDPattern.MatchString(providerID) {\n273|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe provider identifier is not a provider-id\", \"provider_id\")\n274|\t\tif err != nil {\n275|\t\t\treturn Probe{}, err\n276|\t\t}\n277|\t\treturn Probe{}, failure\n278|\t}\n279|\tmanifestDigest, ok := checkDigest(members[\"adapter_manifest_digest\"])\n280|\tif !ok {\n281|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe manifest digest is not a digest\", \"adapter_manifest_digest\")\n282|\t\tif err != nil {\n283|\t\t\treturn Probe{}, err\n284|\t\t}\n285|\t\treturn Probe{}, failure\n286|\t}\n287|\tadapterVersion, ok := rawString(members[\"adapter_version\"])\n288|\tif !ok || !semverPattern.MatchString(adapterVersion) {\n289|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe adapter version is not SemVer\", \"adapter_version\")\n290|\t\tif err != nil {\n291|\t\t\treturn Probe{}, err\n292|\t\t}\n293|\t\treturn Probe{}, failure\n294|\t}\n295|\tenvironment, err := DecodeTuple(members[\"environment\"])\n296|\tif err != nil {\n297|\t\treturn Probe{}, err\n298|\t}\n299|\tcapabilities, err := decodeCapabilities(members[\"capabilities\"])\n300|\tif err != nil {\n301|\t\treturn Probe{}, err\n302|\t}\n303|\twarnings, ok := checkSortedUniqueStrings(members[\"warnings\"], 0, 2048, 0, 1024)\n304|\tif !ok {\n305|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe warnings are not sorted unique string[0..2048][0..1024]\", \"warnings\")\n306|\t\tif err != nil {\n307|\t\t\treturn Probe{}, err\n308|\t\t}\n309|\t\treturn Probe{}, failure\n310|\t}\n311|\tif !checkExtensions(members[\"extensions\"]) {\n312|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe extensions are not reverse-DNS keyed\", \"extensions\")\n313|\t\tif err != nil {\n314|\t\t\treturn Probe{}, err\n315|\t\t}\n316|\t\treturn Probe{}, failure\n317|\t}\n318|\treturn Probe{\n319|\t\tProviderID:     providerID,\n320|\t\tManifestDigest: manifestDigest.String(),\n321|\t\tAdapterVersion: adapterVersion,\n322|\t\tEnvironment:    environment,\n323|\t\tCapabilities:   capabilities,\n324|\t\tWarnings:       warnings,\n325|\t}, nil\n326|}\n327|\n328|// decodeCapabilities validates the closed capability map: exactly\n329|// the fifteen registry names, each with a closed value. The map\n330|// carries no order — names are the keys — so omission and extra\n331|// are the two refused directions, and duplication is already\n332|// refused by the strict decode.\n333|func decodeCapabilities(raw json.RawMessage) (map[string]Capability, error) {\n334|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(bytesTrimSpace(raw))\n335|\tif fault != nil {\n336|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter capabilities \"+fault.detail, \"capabilities\")\n337|\t\tif err != nil {\n338|\t\t\treturn nil, err\n339|\t\t}\n340|\t\treturn nil, failure\n341|\t}\n342|\tif len(members) != len(capabilityOrder) {\n343|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter capabilities do not carry exactly fifteen entries\", \"capabilities\")\n344|\t\tif err != nil {\n345|\t\t\treturn nil, err\n346|\t\t}\n347|\t\treturn nil, failure\n348|\t}\n349|\tcapabilities := make(map[string]Capability, len(capabilityOrder))\n350|\tfor _, name := range capabilityOrder {\n351|\t\trawValue, present := members[name]\n352|\t\tif !present {\n353|\t\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter capabilities omit a registry capability\", name)\n354|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n355|\t\t\t\treturn nil, err\n356|\t\t\t}\n357|\t\t\treturn nil, failure\n358|\t\t}\n359|\t\tvalue, err := decodeCapabilityValue(rawValue, name)\n360|\t\tif err != nil {\n361|\t\t\treturn nil, err\n362|\t\t}\n363|\t\tcapabilities[name] = value\n364|\t}\n365|\treturn capabilities, nil\n366|}\n367|\n368|// ProbeHostFacts are the host-held values the probe must equal:\n369|// the provider identifier and candidate kind from the probe\n370|// request the host built, the manifest digest the host computed,\n371|// and the manifest the host verified. Nothing here comes from the\n372|// adapter.\n373|type ProbeHostFacts struct {\n374|\tExpectedProviderID string\n375|\tExpectedKind       CandidateKind\n376|\tManifestDigest     string\n377|\tManifest           Manifest\n378|}\n379|\n380|// CheckProbe enforces the Section 7.8 probe equalities: provider\n381|// ID, manifest digest, and adapter version equal the verified\n382|// manifest and host values, and the reported tuple is the\n383|// manifest's tuple — the adapter's one semantic native\n384|// environment, so a probe reporting any other tuple is an\n385|// unrequested tuple and is refused. The tuple's adapter version\n386|// must equal the probe's own adapter version: both name the same\n387|// probed software, and a probe disagreeing with itself is\n388|// refused. Whether the tuple's environment version satisfies the\n389|// manifest's version-range constraint language is a stated bound:\n390|// the range grammar has no evaluation rule in Section 7.8.\n391|func CheckProbe(probe Probe, facts ProbeHostFacts) error {\n392|\tif probe.ProviderID != facts.ExpectedProviderID {\n393|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe provider identifier does not match the requested provider\", \"provider_id\")\n394|\t\tif err != nil {\n395|\t\t\treturn err\n396|\t\t}\n397|\t\treturn failure\n398|\t}\n399|\tif probe.ProviderID != facts.Manifest.ProviderID {\n400|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe provider identifier does not match the verified manifest\", \"provider_id\")\n401|\t\tif err != nil {\n402|\t\t\treturn err\n403|\t\t}\n404|\t\treturn failure\n405|\t}\n406|\tif probe.ManifestDigest != facts.ManifestDigest {\n407|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe manifest digest does not match the host-computed digest\", \"adapter_manifest_digest\")\n408|\t\tif err != nil {\n409|\t\t\treturn err\n410|\t\t}\n411|\t\treturn failure\n412|\t}\n413|\tif probe.AdapterVersion != facts.Manifest.AdapterVersion {\n414|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe adapter version does not match the verified manifest\", \"adapter_version\")\n415|\t\tif err != nil {\n416|\t\t\treturn err\n417|\t\t}\n418|\t\treturn failure\n419|\t}\n420|\tif probe.Environment.EnvironmentID != facts.Manifest.EnvironmentID {\n421|\t\tfailure, err := failUnsupportedTuple(\"adapter probe reports a tuple outside the manifest environment\", probe.Environment.EnvironmentID)\n422|\t\tif err != nil {\n423|\t\t\treturn err\n424|\t\t}\n425|\t\treturn failure\n426|\t}\n427|\tif probe.Environment.AdapterVersion != probe.AdapterVersion {\n428|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"adapter probe tuple adapter version does not match the probe adapter version\", \"environment\")\n429|\t\tif err != nil {\n430|\t\t\treturn err\n431|\t\t}\n432|\t\treturn failure\n433|\t}\n434|\treturn nil\n435|}\n436|\n437|// CheckProbeRequest binds the probe request the host built to the\n438|// trusted candidate: the expected provider identifier and\n439|// candidate kind must equal the candidate the host will invoke.\n440|// A request naming a different provider or kind would attest a\n441|// probe for a candidate the host never observed.\n442|func CheckProbeRequest(expectedProviderID string, expectedKind CandidateKind, candidate TrustedCandidate) error {\n443|\tif expectedProviderID != candidate.ProviderID {\n444|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"probe request provider identifier does not match the trusted candidate\", \"expected_provider_id\")\n445|\t\tif err != nil {\n446|\t\t\treturn err\n447|\t\t}\n448|\t\treturn failure\n449|\t}\n450|\tif expectedKind != candidate.Kind {\n451|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"probe request candidate kind does not match the trusted candidate\", \"expected_candidate_kind\")\n452|\t\tif err != nil {\n453|\t\t\treturn err\n454|\t\t}\n455|\t\treturn failure\n456|\t}\n457|\treturn nil\n458|}\n459|\n460|// CapabilityUsable reports whether the named capability is a usable\n461|// surface: present in the closed registry with status=available and\n462|// enabled=true. Conditional, unsupported, and unknown surfaces are\n463|// never usable, and neither is a name outside the registry.\n464|func CapabilityUsable(probe Probe, name string) bool {\n465|\tvalue, present := probe.Capabilities[name]\n466|\tif !present {\n467|\t\treturn false\n468|\t}\n469|\treturn value.Status == \"available\" && value.Enabled\n470|}\n471|\n472|// ProviderCapability is one provider-probe capability the\n473|// target-write gate reads: the provider's portable-store and\n474|// native-resume facts live in the provider probe, not the adapter\n475|// probe, so the caller projects exactly those two surfaces.\n476|type ProviderCapability struct {\n477|\tStatus  string\n478|\tEnabled bool\n479|}\n480|\n481|// CheckTargetWriteGates enforces the Section 7.8 target-write\n482|// conjunction: available canonical-write or official-import,\n483|// native-read-back, native-resume-plan, and workspace-binding on\n484|// the adapter side, plus provider portable-store and native-resume\n485|// on the provider side. Exact execution bindings, accepted\n486|// non-revoked tuple entries, and current fixture plus bounded\n487|// resume-smoke evidence are the caller's adjacent gates\n488|// (CheckBinding, CheckTupleAdmission, CheckDoctorResult): this\n489|// gate decides the capability conjunction only. --force,\n490|// experimental profiles, and environment-name-only matches cannot\n491|// bypass these gates: the function takes no bypass parameter, so a\n492|// caller cannot express one. Unknown sources may be archived only\n493|// after safe byte enumeration; unknown targets never write —\n494|// which this gate enforces by refusing every capability it cannot\n495|// see as available and enabled.\n496|func CheckTargetWriteGates(adapter map[string]Capability, provider map[string]ProviderCapability) error {\n497|\tif !capabilityMapUsable(adapter, \"canonical_write\") && !capabilityMapUsable(adapter, \"official_import\") {\n498|\t\tfailure, err := failCapability(\"target write has neither usable canonical-write nor official-import\", \"canonical_write|official_import\")\n499|\t\tif err != nil {\n500|\t\t\treturn err\n501|\t\t}\n502|\t\treturn failure\n503|\t}\n504|\tfor _, name := range []string{\"native_read_back\", \"native_resume_plan\", \"workspace_binding\"} {\n505|\t\tif !capabilityMapUsable(adapter, name) {\n506|\t\t\tfailure, err := failCapability(\"target write misses a usable adapter capability\", name)\n507|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n508|\t\t\t\treturn err\n509|\t\t\t}\n510|\t\t\treturn failure\n511|\t\t}\n512|\t}\n513|\tfor _, name := range []string{\"portable_store\", \"native_resume\"} {\n514|\t\tvalue, present := provider[name]\n515|\t\tif !present || value.Status != \"available\" || !value.Enabled {\n516|\t\t\tfailure, err := failCapability(\"target write misses a usable provider capability\", \"provider:\"+name)\n517|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n518|\t\t\t\treturn err\n519|\t\t\t}\n520|\t\t\treturn failure\n521|\t\t}\n522|\t}\n523|\treturn nil\n524|}\n525|\n526|// capabilityMapUsable reports whether the named adapter capability\n527|// is usable. An absent name is not usable: the map must be the\n528|// decoded probe map, which always carries all fifteen.\n529|func capabilityMapUsable(adapter map[string]Capability, name string) bool {\n530|\tvalue, present := adapter[name]\n531|\tif !present {\n532|\t\treturn false\n533|\t}\n534|\treturn value.Status == \"available\" && value.Enabled\n535|}\n536|\n537|// doctorResultMembers is the exact doctor success-body member set.\n538|var doctorResultMembers = map[string]bool{\n539|\t\"context\":               true,\n540|\t\"direction\":             true,\n541|\t\"registry_sequence\":     true,\n542|\t\"registry_entry_status\": true,\n543|\t\"findings\":              true,\n544|\t\"healthy\":               true,\n545|\t\"extensions\":            true,\n546|}\n547|\n548|// doctorResultRequired lists doctorResultMembers in order.\n549|var doctorResultRequired = []string{\n550|\t\"context\",\n551|\t\"direction\",\n552|\t\"registry_sequence\",\n553|\t\"registry_entry_status\",\n554|\t\"findings\",\n555|\t\"healthy\",\n556|\t\"extensions\",\n557|}\n558|\n559|// DoctorResult is one validated doctor success body.\n560|type DoctorResult struct {\n561|\tContext          CallContext\n562|\tDirection        Direction\n563|\tRegistrySequence uint64\n564|\tEntryStatus      string\n565|\tFindings         []Finding\n566|\tHealthy          bool\n567|}\n568|\n569|// DecodeDoctorResult validates one closed doctor success body: the\n570|// echoed context, the direction in the closed vocabulary, the\n571|// registry sequence as uint53, the entry status in\n572|// accepted|revoked|absent, the findings, and the health flag. The\n573|// health rule itself is CheckDoctorHealthy: decoding proves shape,\n574|// not health.\n575|func DecodeDoctorResult(body []byte, sent CallContext, sentDirection Direction) (DoctorResult, error) {\n576|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(body)\n577|\tif fault != nil {\n578|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result \"+fault.detail, fault.member)\n579|\t\tif err != nil {\n580|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n581|\t\t}\n582|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n583|\t}\n584|\tif name, unknown := unknownMember(members, doctorResultMembers); unknown {\n585|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result carries unknown member\", name)\n586|\t\tif err != nil {\n587|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n588|\t\t}\n589|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n590|\t}\n591|\tif name, missing := missingMember(members, doctorResultRequired); missing {\n592|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result misses a required member\", name)\n593|\t\tif err != nil {\n594|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n595|\t\t}\n596|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n597|\t}\n598|\tcontext, err := CheckContextEcho(sent, members[\"context\"])\n599|\tif err != nil {\n600|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n601|\t}\n602|\tdirection, ok := rawString(members[\"direction\"])\n603|\tif !ok || !validDirection(direction) {\n604|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result direction is outside source_read|target_write\", \"direction\")\n605|\t\tif err != nil {\n606|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n607|\t\t}\n608|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n609|\t}\n610|\tif Direction(direction) != sentDirection {\n611|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result direction does not answer the request direction\", \"direction\")\n612|\t\tif err != nil {\n613|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n614|\t\t}\n615|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n616|\t}\n617|\tsequence, ok := checkUint53Bounds(members[\"registry_sequence\"], 0, maxUint53)\n618|\tif !ok {\n619|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result registry sequence is not a uint53\", \"registry_sequence\")\n620|\t\tif err != nil {\n621|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n622|\t\t}\n623|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n624|\t}\n625|\tstatus, ok := rawString(members[\"registry_entry_status\"])\n626|\tif !ok || !validRegistryEntryStatus(status) {\n627|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result entry status is outside accepted|revoked|absent\", \"registry_entry_status\")\n628|\t\tif err != nil {\n629|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n630|\t\t}\n631|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n632|\t}\n633|\tfindings, err := DecodeFindings(members[\"findings\"], 4096)\n634|\tif err != nil {\n635|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n636|\t}\n637|\thealthy, ok := rawBool(members[\"healthy\"])\n638|\tif !ok {\n639|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result health flag is not a boolean\", \"healthy\")\n640|\t\tif err != nil {\n641|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n642|\t\t}\n643|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n644|\t}\n645|\tif !checkExtensions(members[\"extensions\"]) {\n646|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"doctor result extensions are not reverse-DNS keyed\", \"extensions\")\n647|\t\tif err != nil {\n648|\t\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, err\n649|\t\t}\n650|\t\treturn DoctorResult{}, failure\n651|\t}\n652|\treturn DoctorResult{\n653|\t\tContext:          context,\n654|\t\tDirection:        Direction(direction),\n655|\t\tRegistrySequence: sequence,\n656|\t\tEntryStatus:      status,\n657|\t\tFindings:         findings,\n658|\t\tHealthy:          healthy,\n659|\t}, nil\n660|}\n661|\n662|// CheckDoctorHealthy enforces the doctor health rule: healthy\n663|// requires an accepted exact binding and every required\n664|// capability. A healthy=true result over a revoked or absent entry\n665|// is refused, and so is a healthy=true result with any required\n666|// capability unusable. healthy=false is always structurally\n667|// admissible: the rule states necessary conditions, not\n668|// sufficient ones. Every required name must belong to the closed\n669|// fifteen-registry; a required set naming anything else is a\n670|// caller error, because the host cannot demand a surface the\n671|// contract never defined.\n672|func CheckDoctorHealthy(result DoctorResult, probe Probe, required []string) error {\n673|\tfor _, name := range required {\n674|\t\tif !validCapabilityName(name) {\n675|\t\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"doctor required set names a capability outside the closed registry\", \"required\")\n676|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n677|\t\t\t\treturn err\n678|\t\t\t}\n679|\t\t\treturn failure\n680|\t\t}\n681|\t}\n682|\tif !result.Healthy {\n683|\t\treturn nil\n684|\t}\n685|\tif result.EntryStatus != \"accepted\" {\n686|\t\tfailure, err := failCapability(\"doctor reports healthy without an accepted registry entry\", \"tuple_registry\")\n687|\t\tif err != nil {\n688|\t\t\treturn err\n689|\t\t}\n690|\t\treturn failure\n691|\t}\n692|\tfor _, name := range required {\n693|\t\tif !CapabilityUsable(probe, name) {\n694|\t\t\tfailure, err := failCapability(\"doctor reports healthy without a usable required capability\", name)\n695|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n696|\t\t\t\treturn err\n697|\t\t\t}\n698|\t\t\treturn failure\n699|\t\t}\n700|\t}\n701|\treturn nil\n702|}\n703|\n704|// validCapabilityName reports whether the name belongs to the\n705|// fifteen-capability registry.\n706|func validCapabilityName(name string) bool {\n707|\tfor _, capability := range capabilityOrder {\n708|\t\tif capability == name {\n709|\t\t\treturn true\n710|\t\t}\n711|\t}\n712|\treturn false\n713|}\n714|\n715|// DoctorRequiredCapabilities returns the closed required-capability\n716|// set for one doctor direction. For target_write it is the Section\n717|// 7.8 target-write adapter set: the import strategy selects which\n718|// member of the canonical-write/official-import pair is required,\n719|// and native-read-back, native-resume-plan, and workspace-binding\n720|// are always required. For source_read it is empty: Section 7.8\n721|// names no per-direction source set, so the caller carries its\n722|// tuple-registry-derived requirements explicitly rather than\n723|// reading them from an invented list. The strategy-to-pair mapping\n724|// is an interpretation recorded here, not a derived rule: the\n725|// target_official_import strategy authorizes the official-import\n726|// member, every other target strategy the canonical-write member.\n727|func DoctorRequiredCapabilities(direction Direction, useOfficialImport bool) []string {\n728|\tif direction != DirectionTargetWrite {\n729|\t\treturn nil\n730|\t}\n731|\twriter := \"canonical_write\"\n732|\tif useOfficialImport {\n733|\t\twriter = \"official_import\"\n734|\t}\n735|\treturn []string{writer, \"native_read_back\", \"native_resume_plan\", \"workspace_binding\"}\n736|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
