{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c743","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07476-3862-7671-a25f-75740245e24f"},"sequence":508,"recorded_at":1780531400001011,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"05fde564-2112-4c57-a4c9-ed3956d2c26c"},"task_id":"05fde564-2112-4c57-a4c9-ed3956d2c26c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"05fde564-2112-4c57-a4c9-ed3956d2c26c","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessadapter/inventory_test.go`.\n1|package sessadapter\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"fmt\"\n5|\t\"go/ast\"\n6|\t\"go/parser\"\n7|\t\"go/token\"\n8|\t\"os\"\n9|\t\"path/filepath\"\n10|\t\"sort\"\n11|\t\"strconv\"\n12|\t\"strings\"\n13|\t\"testing\"\n14|)\n15|\n16|// This file is the derived refusal-arm inventory. It exists\n17|// because a new refusal through an existing site — a widened\n18|// member set, a new detail literal, a dropped check that slides\n19|// to a lower arm — leaves the whole suite green unless the arm\n20|// set is derived from production source by parsing it, never by\n21|// listing it.\n22|//\n23|// Derivation (deriveRefusalArms): every call to one of the seven\n24|// refusal constructors with a string-literal first argument\n25|// yields ctor|<constructor>|<detail>; a call whose first\n26|// argument is a literal prefix plus fault.detail yields\n27|// ctor|<constructor>|conduit|<function>|<prefix>, so conduits in\n28|// different functions never merge; every &frameFault{...}\n29|// literal yields frame|<detail>. A constructor call with any\n30|// other first-argument shape lands as\n31|// ctor|<constructor>|expr|<function> rather than passing\n32|// silently. Constructor references outside direct-call position\n33|// fail the derivation outright: an aliased constructor hides\n34|// every arm it builds. All three alias spellings are caught —\n35|// `alias := failInvalid`, `var alias = failInvalid` at package\n36|// level, and `var alias = failInvalid` inside a function body —\n37|// because the gate exempts only the definition's own Name in its\n38|// ValueSpec, never a constructor identifier appearing as a\n39|// ValueSpec value. The constructors of this package are\n40|// themselves declared as `var failX = func...`, so their\n41|// definition Names must stay exempt while any other var-held\n42|// reference fails.\n43|// Package-level var initializers scan under their variable name,\n44|// so a refusal arm hiding in a package-level func literal is\n45|// derived, not missed.\n46|//\n47|// The constructor denominator is itself derived, not listed on\n48|// trust: TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction requires the\n49|// registered set to equal the package-level vars whose bodies\n50|// call axerror.New, and every axerror.New site in production to\n51|// sit inside one registered body. An eighth constructor or an\n52|// inline axerror.New refusal carries an additive arm the\n53|// derivation never observes, and fails there instead of passing\n54|// silently.\n55|//\n56|// Both directions are checked:\n57|// TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed (every derived arm\n58|// carries a witness) and TestWitnessedArmsAreAllDerived (every\n59|// witness names a derived arm, so a truncated derivation reddens\n60|// on the orphaned witnesses instead of passing vacuously).\n61|// TestEveryArmWitnessRefusesAtTheProductionEntry drives each\n62|// witness through the production entry and requires the refusal\n63|// to come from the arm under test: code, distinguishing detail,\n64|// and rule text. Empty, single-file, or unparseable derivations\n65|// fail closed: a domain that silently derives nothing is not a\n66|// measurement.\n67|//\n68|// Stated bounds: the five timestamp pairs share one\n69|// (constructor, detail) identity across their checkTimestamp and\n70|// Time halves by construction (one rule, two halves); deleting\n71|// one half is a behavioral mutant the entry-point tests must\n72|// catch, and every witness below proves both halves. Arms\n73|// sharing one identity merge to one obligation only there and\n74|// nowhere else: any other merge fails the derivation. The\n75|// open-class member gates (unknown-member and duplicate-member\n76|// refusals) range over an unbounded name class, so one witness\n77|// per arm proves the gate fires, not that every name is gated:\n78|// a mutant exempting a different name than the witnessed one is\n79|// outside what the arm inventory narrows, and is recorded here\n80|// rather than proven.\n81|\n82|// refusalArmCensusFloor is the derived arm count this test was\n83|// written against. It is a tripwire, not an enumeration: a\n84|// derivation returning fewer arms fails closed even when every\n85|// surviving arm is witnessed, which is what catches a silently\n86|// truncated scan. Raising it is routine when production gains a\n87|// refusal; lowering it requires saying why.\n88|const refusalArmCensusFloor = 323\n89|\n90|// refusalConstructors is the closed constructor set the\n91|// derivation observes, pinned against production by\n92|// TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction: the registered names\n93|// must equal the package-level error-constructing vars exactly,\n94|// and every axerror.New site in production must sit inside one\n95|// registered constructor body. A refusal built any other way —\n96|// through an unregistered eighth constructor or an inline\n97|// axerror.New — fails that census; a refusal built through an\n98|// aliased constructor fails the alias gate below.\n99|var refusalConstructors = []string{\n100|\t\"failInvalid\",\n101|\t\"failProtocol\",\n102|\t\"failUnknownOperation\",\n103|\t\"failCapability\",\n104|\t\"failUnavailable\",\n105|\t\"failUnsupportedTuple\",\n106|\t\"failIntegrity\",\n107|}\n108|\n109|func deriveRefusalArms(t *testing.T) map[string]struct{} {\n110|\tt.Helper()\n111|\tdirectory, err := os.Getwd()\n112|\tif err != nil {\n113|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive refusal arms: %v\", err)\n114|\t}\n115|\tarms, scanned, err := refusalArmsIn(directory)\n116|\tif err != nil {\n117|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive refusal arms: %v\", err)\n118|\t}\n119|\tif len(scanned) == 0 {\n120|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived refusal arms from zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n121|\t}\n122|\tif len(arms) == 0 {\n123|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero refusal arms from the package sources; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n124|\t}\n125|\tif len(arms) < refusalArmCensusFloor {\n126|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derived %d refusal arms, below the %d census floor; the derivation is short, not the package\", len(arms), refusalArmCensusFloor)\n127|\t}\n128|\tt.Logf(\"refusal arm coverage domain: %d derived arms across %d production files\", len(arms), len(scanned))\n129|\treturn arms\n130|}\n131|\n132|func refusalArmsIn(directory string) (map[string]struct{}, []string, error) {\n133|\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(directory)\n134|\tif err != nil {\n135|\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n136|\t}\n137|\tarms := map[string]struct{}{}\n138|\tvar scanned []string\n139|\tconstructors := map[string]bool{}\n140|\tfor _, name := range refusalConstructors {\n141|\t\tconstructors[name] = true\n142|\t}\n143|\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n144|\t\tname := entry.Name()\n145|\t\tif entry.IsDir() || !strings.HasSuffix(name, \".go\") || strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n146|\t\t\tcontinue\n147|\t\t}\n148|\t\tscanned = append(scanned, name)\n149|\t\tpath := filepath.Join(directory, name)\n150|\t\tsource, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n151|\t\tif err != nil {\n152|\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n153|\t\t}\n154|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n155|\t\tsyntax, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, path, source, 0)\n156|\t\tif err != nil {\n157|\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n158|\t\t}\n159|\t\tif err := collectFileArms(fileSet, syntax, constructors, arms); err != nil {\n160|\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n161|\t\t}\n162|\t}\n163|\treturn arms, scanned, nil\n164|}\n165|\n166|// TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction pins the constructor\n167|// denominator against production source in both directions: the\n168|// set of package-level func-valued vars whose body constructs\n169|// an error with axerror.New must equal refusalConstructors\n170|// exactly, and every axerror.New call in production must sit\n171|// inside one registered constructor body. The arm inventory\n172|// observes only registered constructors, so an eighth\n173|// constructor with an additive arm, or an inline axerror.New\n174|// refusal with an additive arm, both survive the full suite —\n175|// and both fail here, the first as an unregistered constructor,\n176|// the second as a construction site outside every registered\n177|// body. axerror.Decode is a read, not a construction, and is\n178|// ignored. An empty scan fails closed.\n179|func TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction(t *testing.T) {\n180|\tdirectory, err := os.Getwd()\n181|\tif err != nil {\n182|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"constructor census: %v\", err)\n183|\t}\n184|\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(directory)\n185|\tif err != nil {\n186|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"constructor census: %v\", err)\n187|\t}\n188|\tregistered := map[string]bool{}\n189|\tfor _, name := range refusalConstructors {\n190|\t\tregistered[name] = true\n191|\t}\n192|\tproduced := map[string]string{}\n193|\tscanned := 0\n194|\tvar violations []string\n195|\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n196|\t\tname := entry.Name()\n197|\t\tif entry.IsDir() || !strings.HasSuffix(name, \".go\") || strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n198|\t\t\tcontinue\n199|\t\t}\n200|\t\tscanned++\n201|\t\tpath := filepath.Join(directory, name)\n202|\t\tsource, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n203|\t\tif err != nil {\n204|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"constructor census: %v\", err)\n205|\t\t}\n206|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n207|\t\tsyntax, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, path, source, 0)\n208|\t\tif err != nil {\n209|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"constructor census: %v\", err)\n210|\t\t}\n211|\t\tfor _, violation := range constructorSitesInFile(fileSet, syntax, registered, produced, name) {\n212|\t\t\tviolations = append(violations, name+\": \"+violation)\n213|\t\t}\n214|\t}\n215|\tif scanned == 0 {\n216|\t\tt.Fatal(\"constructor census scanned zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n217|\t}\n218|\tsort.Strings(violations)\n219|\tif len(violations) > 0 {\n220|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"error-construction site(s) outside the registered constructors:\\n  %s\", strings.Join(violations, \"\\n  \"))\n221|\t}\n222|\tvar unregistered []string\n223|\tfor name, file := range produced {\n224|\t\tif !registered[name] {\n225|\t\t\tunregistered = append(unregistered, name+\" (\"+file+\")\")\n226|\t\t}\n227|\t}\n228|\tvar orphaned []string\n229|\tfor name := range registered {\n230|\t\tif _, ok := produced[name]; !ok {\n231|\t\t\torphaned = append(orphaned, name)\n232|\t\t}\n233|\t}\n234|\tsort.Strings(unregistered)\n235|\tsort.Strings(orphaned)\n236|\tif len(unregistered) > 0 {\n237|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"production error constructor(s) with no census registration:\\n  %s\", strings.Join(unregistered, \"\\n  \"))\n238|\t}\n239|\tif len(orphaned) > 0 {\n240|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"census registration(s) naming no production constructor:\\n  %s\", strings.Join(orphaned, \"\\n  \"))\n241|\t}\n242|\tt.Logf(\"constructor census: %d constructors across %d files\", len(produced), scanned)\n243|}\n244|\n245|// constructorVarScope is one var-held func literal an\n246|// axerror.New call can attribute to: the holding variable name\n247|// with its source range, and whether the declaration is\n248|// package-level. Only a package-level scope holding a\n249|// registered name is a constructor; anything else enclosing a\n250|// New call is an unregistered construction site.\n251|type constructorVarScope struct {\n252|\tname       string\n253|\tstart, end token.Pos\n254|\ttopLevel   bool\n255|}\n256|\n257|// constructorSitesInFile records every package-level func-valued\n258|// var whose body calls axerror.New into produced, and reports\n259|// every axerror.New call outside a registered constructor body:\n260|// outside any var-held literal, or inside one whose variable is\n261|// not registered. Function-local var-held literals are never\n262|// constructors, so a New call inside one always reports.\n263|func constructorSitesInFile(fileSet *token.FileSet, syntax *ast.File, registered map[string]bool, produced map[string]string, filename string) []string {\n264|\tvar scopes []constructorVarScope\n265|\tvar calls []token.Pos\n266|\tvar stack []ast.Node\n267|\tfuncDepth := 0\n268|\tast.Inspect(syntax, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n269|\t\tif node == nil {\n270|\t\t\tpopped := stack[len(stack)-1]\n271|\t\t\tswitch popped.(type) {\n272|\t\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl, *ast.FuncLit:\n273|\t\t\t\tfuncDepth--\n274|\t\t\t}\n275|\t\t\tstack = stack[:len(stack)-1]\n276|\t\t\treturn true\n277|\t\t}\n278|\t\tswitch node := node.(type) {\n279|\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl, *ast.FuncLit:\n280|\t\t\tfuncDepth++\n281|\t\tcase *ast.GenDecl:\n282|\t\t\tif node.Tok != token.VAR {\n283|\t\t\t\tbreak\n284|\t\t\t}\n285|\t\t\ttopLevel := funcDepth == 0\n286|\t\t\tfor _, specification := range node.Specs {\n287|\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := specification.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n288|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n289|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n290|\t\t\t\t}\n291|\t\t\t\tfor index, ident := range value.Names {\n292|\t\t\t\t\tliteral := pairedFuncLit(value, index)\n293|\t\t\t\t\tif literal == nil {\n294|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n295|\t\t\t\t\t}\n296|\t\t\t\t\tscopes = append(scopes, constructorVarScope{name: ident.Name, start: literal.Pos(), end: literal.End(), topLevel: topLevel})\n297|\t\t\t\t}\n298|\t\t\t}\n299|\t\tcase *ast.CallExpr:\n300|\t\t\tselector, ok := node.Fun.(*ast.SelectorExpr)\n301|\t\t\tif !ok {\n302|\t\t\t\tbreak\n303|\t\t\t}\n304|\t\t\treceiver, ok := selector.X.(*ast.Ident)\n305|\t\t\tif !ok || receiver.Name != \"axerror\" || selector.Sel.Name != \"New\" {\n306|\t\t\t\tbreak\n307|\t\t\t}\n308|\t\t\tcalls = append(calls, node.Pos())\n309|\t\t}\n310|\t\tstack = append(stack, node)\n311|\t\treturn true\n312|\t})\n313|\tvar violations []string\n314|\tfor _, position := range calls {\n315|\t\tbest := \"\"\n316|\t\tvar bestStart token.Pos\n317|\t\tinitialized := false\n318|\t\ttopLevel := false\n319|\t\tfor _, scope := range scopes {\n320|\t\t\tif scope.start <= position && position <= scope.end {\n321|\t\t\t\tif !initialized || scope.start >= bestStart {\n322|\t\t\t\t\tbest, bestStart, initialized, topLevel = scope.name, scope.start, true, scope.topLevel\n323|\t\t\t\t}\n324|\t\t\t}\n325|\t\t}\n326|\t\tswitch {\n327|\t\tcase !initialized:\n328|\t\t\tviolations = append(violations, fmt.Sprintf(\"axerror.New outside any constructor at %s\", fileSet.Position(position)))\n329|\t\tcase !registered[best]:\n330|\t\t\tviolations = append(violations, fmt.Sprintf(\"axerror.New inside unregistered %q at %s\", best, fileSet.Position(position)))\n331|\t\tcase topLevel:\n332|\t\t\tproduced[best] = filename\n333|\t\t}\n334|\t}\n335|\treturn violations\n336|}\n337|\n338|// pairedFuncLit returns the func literal holding one ValueSpec\n339|// name: the index-paired value when every name carries its own,\n340|// the shared value when one serves all names, and nil for any\n341|// other shape or a non-literal value.\n342|func pairedFuncLit(value *ast.ValueSpec, index int) *ast.FuncLit {\n343|\tvar candidate ast.Expr\n344|\tswitch {\n345|\tcase len(value.Values) == len(value.Names) && index < len(value.Values):\n346|\t\tcandidate = value.Values[index]\n347|\tcase len(value.Values) == 1:\n348|\t\tcandidate = value.Values[0]\n349|\tdefault:\n350|\t\treturn nil\n351|\t}\n352|\tliteral, ok := candidate.(*ast.FuncLit)\n353|\tif !ok {\n354|\t\treturn nil\n355|\t}\n356|\treturn literal\n357|}\n358|\n359|// scopeRange is one named scope constructor calls attribute to:\n360|// a function declaration or a package-level variable holding a\n361|// func literal.\n362|type scopeRange struct {\n363|\tname       string\n364|\tstart, end token.Pos\n365|}\n366|\n367|// collectFileArms derives every arm in one production file from a\n368|// single parse, so scope containment compares positions within\n369|// one file set: constructor calls attribute to their innermost\n370|// enclosing scope by source range, frameFault literals derive\n371|// frame arms, and any constructor identifier outside call-fun\n372|// and definition position is an alias and fails the file.\n373|func collectFileArms(fileSet *token.FileSet, syntax *ast.File, constructors map[string]bool, arms map[string]struct{}) error {\n374|\tvar scopes []scopeRange\n375|\ttype pendingCall struct {\n376|\t\tname     string\n377|\t\tcall     *ast.CallExpr\n378|\t\tposition token.Pos\n379|\t}\n380|\tvar calls []pendingCall\n381|\tvar frames []*ast.CompositeLit\n382|\ttype identUse struct {\n383|\t\tidentifier *ast.Ident\n384|\t\tparent     ast.Node\n385|\t}\n386|\tvar uses []identUse\n387|\tvar stack []ast.Node\n388|\tast.Inspect(syntax, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n389|\t\tif node == nil {\n390|\t\t\tstack = stack[:len(stack)-1]\n391|\t\t\treturn true\n392|\t\t}\n393|\t\tvar parent ast.Node\n394|\t\tif len(stack) > 0 {\n395|\t\t\tparent = stack[len(stack)-1]\n396|\t\t}\n397|\t\tswitch node := node.(type) {\n398|\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl:\n399|\t\t\tscopes = append(scopes, scopeRange{name: node.Name.Name, start: node.Pos(), end: node.End()})\n400|\t\tcase *ast.GenDecl:\n401|\t\t\tfor _, specification := range node.Specs {\n402|\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := specification.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n403|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n404|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n405|\t\t\t\t}\n406|\t\t\t\tfor index, name := range value.Names {\n407|\t\t\t\t\tif index < len(value.Values) {\n408|\t\t\t\t\t\tif literal, ok := value.Values[index].(*ast.FuncLit); ok {\n409|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tscopes = append(scopes, scopeRange{name: \"var:\" + name.Name, start: literal.Pos(), end: literal.End()})\n410|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n411|\t\t\t\t\t}\n412|\t\t\t\t}\n413|\t\t\t}\n414|\t\tcase *ast.Ident:\n415|\t\t\tif constructors[node.Name] {\n416|\t\t\t\tuses = append(uses, identUse{identifier: node, parent: parent})\n417|\t\t\t}\n418|\t\tcase *ast.CallExpr:\n419|\t\t\tif fun, ok := node.Fun.(*ast.Ident); ok && constructors[fun.Name] {\n420|\t\t\t\tcalls = append(calls, pendingCall{name: fun.Name, call: node, position: node.Pos()})\n421|\t\t\t}\n422|\t\tcase *ast.CompositeLit:\n423|\t\t\tif identifier, ok := node.Type.(*ast.Ident); ok && identifier.Name == \"frameFault\" {\n424|\t\t\t\tframes = append(frames, node)\n425|\t\t\t}\n426|\t\t}\n427|\t\tstack = append(stack, node)\n428|\t\treturn true\n429|\t})\n430|\tfor _, use := range uses {\n431|\t\tif call, ok := use.parent.(*ast.CallExpr); ok {\n432|\t\t\tif fun, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.Ident); ok && fun == use.identifier {\n433|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n434|\t\t\t}\n435|\t\t}\n436|\t\tif specification, ok := use.parent.(*ast.ValueSpec); ok {\n437|\t\t\tdefined := false\n438|\t\t\tfor _, name := range specification.Names {\n439|\t\t\t\tif name == use.identifier {\n440|\t\t\t\t\tdefined = true\n441|\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n442|\t\t\t\t}\n443|\t\t\t}\n444|\t\t\tif defined {\n445|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n446|\t\t\t}\n447|\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"constructor alias of %s buries every arm it builds at %s\", use.identifier.Name, fileSet.Position(use.identifier.Pos()))\n448|\t\t}\n449|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"constructor alias or indirect use of %s at %s\", use.identifier.Name, fileSet.Position(use.identifier.Pos()))\n450|\t}\n451|\tenclosing := func(position token.Pos) string {\n452|\t\tbest := \"package\"\n453|\t\tvar bestStart token.Pos\n454|\t\tinitialized := false\n455|\t\tfor _, scope := range scopes {\n456|\t\t\tif scope.start <= position && position <= scope.end {\n457|\t\t\t\tif !initialized || scope.start >= bestStart {\n458|\t\t\t\t\tbest, bestStart, initialized = scope.name, scope.start, true\n459|\t\t\t\t}\n460|\t\t\t}\n461|\t\t}\n462|\t\treturn best\n463|\t}\n464|\tfor _, call := range calls {\n465|\t\tarm, err := callArm(call.name, call.call, enclosing(call.position))\n466|\t\tif err != nil {\n467|\t\t\treturn err\n468|\t\t}\n469|\t\tarms[arm] = struct{}{}\n470|\t}\n471|\tfor _, frame := range frames {\n472|\t\tdetail, err := frameDetail(frame)\n473|\t\tif err != nil {\n474|\t\t\treturn err\n475|\t\t}\n476|\t\tarms[\"frame|\"+detail] = struct{}{}\n477|\t}\n478|\treturn nil\n479|}\n480|\n481|// callArm derives one constructor arm: a string-literal first\n482|// argument is the detail; a literal-plus-fault.detail binary is a\n483|// conduit keyed by function and prefix; anything else is an\n484|// expr obligation keyed by function.\n485|func callArm(constructor string, call *ast.CallExpr, function string) (string, error) {\n486|\tif len(call.Args) == 0 {\n487|\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"constructor %s called with no arguments in %s\", constructor, function)\n488|\t}\n489|\tswitch first := call.Args[0].(type) {\n490|\tcase *ast.BasicLit:\n491|\t\tif first.Kind != token.STRING {\n492|\t\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"constructor %s first argument is not a string in %s\", constructor, function)\n493|\t\t}\n494|\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(first.Value)\n495|\t\tif err != nil {\n496|\t\t\treturn \"\", err\n497|\t\t}\n498|\t\treturn \"ctor|\" + constructor + \"|\" + detail, nil\n499|\tcase *ast.BinaryExpr:\n500|\t\tprefix, ok := first.X.(*ast.BasicLit)\n(more lines below)"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c745","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07476-3862-7671-a25f-75740245e24f"},"sequence":509,"recorded_at":1780531400001013,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"05fde564-2112-4c57-a4c9-ed3956d2c26c"},"task_id":"05fde564-2112-4c57-a4c9-ed3956d2c26c","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"05fde564-2112-4c57-a4c9-ed3956d2c26c"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c747","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07476-3862-7671-a25f-75740245e24f"},"sequence":510,"recorded_at":1780531400001015,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a"},"call_id":"call_01a0747744fe7b828cc764f90de7db01","text":"Read text file `internal/sessadapter/inventory_test.go`.\n1|package sessadapter\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"fmt\"\n5|\t\"go/ast\"\n6|\t\"go/parser\"\n7|\t\"go/token\"\n8|\t\"os\"\n9|\t\"path/filepath\"\n10|\t\"sort\"\n11|\t\"strconv\"\n12|\t\"strings\"\n13|\t\"testing\"\n14|)\n15|\n16|// This file is the derived refusal-arm inventory. It exists\n17|// because a new refusal through an existing site — a widened\n18|// member set, a new detail literal, a dropped check that slides\n19|// to a lower arm — leaves the whole suite green unless the arm\n20|// set is derived from production source by parsing it, never by\n21|// listing it.\n22|//\n23|// Derivation (deriveRefusalArms): every call to one of the seven\n24|// refusal constructors with a string-literal first argument\n25|// yields ctor|<constructor>|<detail>; a call whose first\n26|// argument is a literal prefix plus fault.detail yields\n27|// ctor|<constructor>|conduit|<function>|<prefix>, so conduits in\n28|// different functions never merge; every &frameFault{...}\n29|// literal yields frame|<detail>. A constructor call with any\n30|// other first-argument shape lands as\n31|// ctor|<constructor>|expr|<function> rather than passing\n32|// silently. Constructor references outside direct-call position\n33|// fail the derivation outright: an aliased constructor hides\n34|// every arm it builds. All three alias spellings are caught —\n35|// `alias := failInvalid`, `var alias = failInvalid` at package\n36|// level, and `var alias = failInvalid` inside a function body —\n37|// because the gate exempts only the definition's own Name in its\n38|// ValueSpec, never a constructor identifier appearing as a\n39|// ValueSpec value. The constructors of this package are\n40|// themselves declared as `var failX = func...`, so their\n41|// definition Names must stay exempt while any other var-held\n42|// reference fails.\n43|// Package-level var initializers scan under their variable name,\n44|// so a refusal arm hiding in a package-level func literal is\n45|// derived, not missed.\n46|//\n47|// The constructor denominator is itself derived, not listed on\n48|// trust: TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction requires the\n49|// registered set to equal the package-level vars whose bodies\n50|// call axerror.New, and every axerror.New site in production to\n51|// sit inside one registered body. An eighth constructor or an\n52|// inline axerror.New refusal carries an additive arm the\n53|// derivation never observes, and fails there instead of passing\n54|// silently.\n55|//\n56|// Both directions are checked:\n57|// TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed (every derived arm\n58|// carries a witness) and TestWitnessedArmsAreAllDerived (every\n59|// witness names a derived arm, so a truncated derivation reddens\n60|// on the orphaned witnesses instead of passing vacuously).\n61|// TestEveryArmWitnessRefusesAtTheProductionEntry drives each\n62|// witness through the production entry and requires the refusal\n63|// to come from the arm under test: code, distinguishing detail,\n64|// and rule text. Empty, single-file, or unparseable derivations\n65|// fail closed: a domain that silently derives nothing is not a\n66|// measurement.\n67|//\n68|// Stated bounds: the five timestamp pairs share one\n69|// (constructor, detail) identity across their checkTimestamp and\n70|// Time halves by construction (one rule, two halves); deleting\n71|// one half is a behavioral mutant the entry-point tests must\n72|// catch, and every witness below proves both halves. Arms\n73|// sharing one identity merge to one obligation only there and\n74|// nowhere else: any other merge fails the derivation. The\n75|// open-class member gates (unknown-member and duplicate-member\n76|// refusals) range over an unbounded name class, so one witness\n77|// per arm proves the gate fires, not that every name is gated:\n78|// a mutant exempting a different name than the witnessed one is\n79|// outside what the arm inventory narrows, and is recorded here\n80|// rather than proven.\n81|\n82|// refusalArmCensusFloor is the derived arm count this test was\n83|// written against. It is a tripwire, not an enumeration: a\n84|// derivation returning fewer arms fails closed even when every\n85|// surviving arm is witnessed, which is what catches a silently\n86|// truncated scan. Raising it is routine when production gains a\n87|// refusal; lowering it requires saying why.\n88|const refusalArmCensusFloor = 323\n89|\n90|// refusalConstructors is the closed constructor set the\n91|// derivation observes, pinned against production by\n92|// TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction: the registered names\n93|// must equal the package-level error-constructing vars exactly,\n94|// and every axerror.New site in production must sit inside one\n95|// registered constructor body. A refusal built any other way —\n96|// through an unregistered eighth constructor or an inline\n97|// axerror.New — fails that census; a refusal built through an\n98|// aliased constructor fails the alias gate below.\n99|var refusalConstructors = []string{\n100|\t\"failInvalid\",\n101|\t\"failProtocol\",\n102|\t\"failUnknownOperation\",\n103|\t\"failCapability\",\n104|\t\"failUnavailable\",\n105|\t\"failUnsupportedTuple\",\n106|\t\"failIntegrity\",\n107|}\n108|\n109|func deriveRefusalArms(t *testing.T) map[string]struct{} {\n110|\tt.Helper()\n111|\tdirectory, err := os.Getwd()\n112|\tif err != nil {\n113|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive refusal arms: %v\", err)\n114|\t}\n115|\tarms, scanned, err := refusalArmsIn(directory)\n116|\tif err != nil {\n117|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive refusal arms: %v\", err)\n118|\t}\n119|\tif len(scanned) == 0 {\n120|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived refusal arms from zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n121|\t}\n122|\tif len(arms) == 0 {\n123|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero refusal arms from the package sources; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n124|\t}\n125|\tif len(arms) < refusalArmCensusFloor {\n126|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derived %d refusal arms, below the %d census floor; the derivation is short, not the package\", len(arms), refusalArmCensusFloor)\n127|\t}\n128|\tt.Logf(\"refusal arm coverage domain: %d derived arms across %d production files\", len(arms), len(scanned))\n129|\treturn arms\n130|}\n131|\n132|func refusalArmsIn(directory string) (map[string]struct{}, []string, error) {\n133|\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(directory)\n134|\tif err != nil {\n135|\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n136|\t}\n137|\tarms := map[string]struct{}{}\n138|\tvar scanned []string\n139|\tconstructors := map[string]bool{}\n140|\tfor _, name := range refusalConstructors {\n141|\t\tconstructors[name] = true\n142|\t}\n143|\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n144|\t\tname := entry.Name()\n145|\t\tif entry.IsDir() || !strings.HasSuffix(name, \".go\") || strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n146|\t\t\tcontinue\n147|\t\t}\n148|\t\tscanned = append(scanned, name)\n149|\t\tpath := filepath.Join(directory, name)\n150|\t\tsource, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n151|\t\tif err != nil {\n152|\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n153|\t\t}\n154|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n155|\t\tsyntax, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, path, source, 0)\n156|\t\tif err != nil {\n157|\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n158|\t\t}\n159|\t\tif err := collectFileArms(fileSet, syntax, constructors, arms); err != nil {\n160|\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n161|\t\t}\n162|\t}\n163|\treturn arms, scanned, nil\n164|}\n165|\n166|// TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction pins the constructor\n167|// denominator against production source in both directions: the\n168|// set of package-level func-valued vars whose body constructs\n169|// an error with axerror.New must equal refusalConstructors\n170|// exactly, and every axerror.New call in production must sit\n171|// inside one registered constructor body. The arm inventory\n172|// observes only registered constructors, so an eighth\n173|// constructor with an additive arm, or an inline axerror.New\n174|// refusal with an additive arm, both survive the full suite —\n175|// and both fail here, the first as an unregistered constructor,\n176|// the second as a construction site outside every registered\n177|// body. axerror.Decode is a read, not a construction, and is\n178|// ignored. An empty scan fails closed.\n179|func TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction(t *testing.T) {\n180|\tdirectory, err := os.Getwd()\n181|\tif err != nil {\n182|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"constructor census: %v\", err)\n183|\t}\n184|\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(directory)\n185|\tif err != nil {\n186|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"constructor census: %v\", err)\n187|\t}\n188|\tregistered := map[string]bool{}\n189|\tfor _, name := range refusalConstructors {\n190|\t\tregistered[name] = true\n191|\t}\n192|\tproduced := map[string]string{}\n193|\tscanned := 0\n194|\tvar violations []string\n195|\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n196|\t\tname := entry.Name()\n197|\t\tif entry.IsDir() || !strings.HasSuffix(name, \".go\") || strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n198|\t\t\tcontinue\n199|\t\t}\n200|\t\tscanned++\n201|\t\tpath := filepath.Join(directory, name)\n202|\t\tsource, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n203|\t\tif err != nil {\n204|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"constructor census: %v\", err)\n205|\t\t}\n206|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n207|\t\tsyntax, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, path, source, 0)\n208|\t\tif err != nil {\n209|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"constructor census: %v\", err)\n210|\t\t}\n211|\t\tfor _, violation := range constructorSitesInFile(fileSet, syntax, registered, produced, name) {\n212|\t\t\tviolations = append(violations, name+\": \"+violation)\n213|\t\t}\n214|\t}\n215|\tif scanned == 0 {\n216|\t\tt.Fatal(\"constructor census scanned zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n217|\t}\n218|\tsort.Strings(violations)\n219|\tif len(violations) > 0 {\n220|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"error-construction site(s) outside the registered constructors:\\n  %s\", strings.Join(violations, \"\\n  \"))\n221|\t}\n222|\tvar unregistered []string\n223|\tfor name, file := range produced {\n224|\t\tif !registered[name] {\n225|\t\t\tunregistered = append(unregistered, name+\" (\"+file+\")\")\n226|\t\t}\n227|\t}\n228|\tvar orphaned []string\n229|\tfor name := range registered {\n230|\t\tif _, ok := produced[name]; !ok {\n231|\t\t\torphaned = append(orphaned, name)\n232|\t\t}\n233|\t}\n234|\tsort.Strings(unregistered)\n235|\tsort.Strings(orphaned)\n236|\tif len(unregistered) > 0 {\n237|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"production error constructor(s) with no census registration:\\n  %s\", strings.Join(unregistered, \"\\n  \"))\n238|\t}\n239|\tif len(orphaned) > 0 {\n240|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"census registration(s) naming no production constructor:\\n  %s\", strings.Join(orphaned, \"\\n  \"))\n241|\t}\n242|\tt.Logf(\"constructor census: %d constructors across %d files\", len(produced), scanned)\n243|}\n244|\n245|// constructorVarScope is one var-held func literal an\n246|// axerror.New call can attribute to: the holding variable name\n247|// with its source range, and whether the declaration is\n248|// package-level. Only a package-level scope holding a\n249|// registered name is a constructor; anything else enclosing a\n250|// New call is an unregistered construction site.\n251|type constructorVarScope struct {\n252|\tname       string\n253|\tstart, end token.Pos\n254|\ttopLevel   bool\n255|}\n256|\n257|// constructorSitesInFile records every package-level func-valued\n258|// var whose body calls axerror.New into produced, and reports\n259|// every axerror.New call outside a registered constructor body:\n260|// outside any var-held literal, or inside one whose variable is\n261|// not registered. Function-local var-held literals are never\n262|// constructors, so a New call inside one always reports.\n263|func constructorSitesInFile(fileSet *token.FileSet, syntax *ast.File, registered map[string]bool, produced map[string]string, filename string) []string {\n264|\tvar scopes []constructorVarScope\n265|\tvar calls []token.Pos\n266|\tvar stack []ast.Node\n267|\tfuncDepth := 0\n268|\tast.Inspect(syntax, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n269|\t\tif node == nil {\n270|\t\t\tpopped := stack[len(stack)-1]\n271|\t\t\tswitch popped.(type) {\n272|\t\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl, *ast.FuncLit:\n273|\t\t\t\tfuncDepth--\n274|\t\t\t}\n275|\t\t\tstack = stack[:len(stack)-1]\n276|\t\t\treturn true\n277|\t\t}\n278|\t\tswitch node := node.(type) {\n279|\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl, *ast.FuncLit:\n280|\t\t\tfuncDepth++\n281|\t\tcase *ast.GenDecl:\n282|\t\t\tif node.Tok != token.VAR {\n283|\t\t\t\tbreak\n284|\t\t\t}\n285|\t\t\ttopLevel := funcDepth == 0\n286|\t\t\tfor _, specification := range node.Specs {\n287|\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := specification.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n288|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n289|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n290|\t\t\t\t}\n291|\t\t\t\tfor index, ident := range value.Names {\n292|\t\t\t\t\tliteral := pairedFuncLit(value, index)\n293|\t\t\t\t\tif literal == nil {\n294|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n295|\t\t\t\t\t}\n296|\t\t\t\t\tscopes = append(scopes, constructorVarScope{name: ident.Name, start: literal.Pos(), end: literal.End(), topLevel: topLevel})\n297|\t\t\t\t}\n298|\t\t\t}\n299|\t\tcase *ast.CallExpr:\n300|\t\t\tselector, ok := node.Fun.(*ast.SelectorExpr)\n301|\t\t\tif !ok {\n302|\t\t\t\tbreak\n303|\t\t\t}\n304|\t\t\treceiver, ok := selector.X.(*ast.Ident)\n305|\t\t\tif !ok || receiver.Name != \"axerror\" || selector.Sel.Name != \"New\" {\n306|\t\t\t\tbreak\n307|\t\t\t}\n308|\t\t\tcalls = append(calls, node.Pos())\n309|\t\t}\n310|\t\tstack = append(stack, node)\n311|\t\treturn true\n312|\t})\n313|\tvar violations []string\n314|\tfor _, position := range calls {\n315|\t\tbest := \"\"\n316|\t\tvar bestStart token.Pos\n317|\t\tinitialized := false\n318|\t\ttopLevel := false\n319|\t\tfor _, scope := range scopes {\n320|\t\t\tif scope.start <= position && position <= scope.end {\n321|\t\t\t\tif !initialized || scope.start >= bestStart {\n322|\t\t\t\t\tbest, bestStart, initialized, topLevel = scope.name, scope.start, true, scope.topLevel\n323|\t\t\t\t}\n324|\t\t\t}\n325|\t\t}\n326|\t\tswitch {\n327|\t\tcase !initialized:\n328|\t\t\tviolations = append(violations, fmt.Sprintf(\"axerror.New outside any constructor at %s\", fileSet.Position(position)))\n329|\t\tcase !registered[best]:\n330|\t\t\tviolations = append(violations, fmt.Sprintf(\"axerror.New inside unregistered %q at %s\", best, fileSet.Position(position)))\n331|\t\tcase topLevel:\n332|\t\t\tproduced[best] = filename\n333|\t\t}\n334|\t}\n335|\treturn violations\n336|}\n337|\n338|// pairedFuncLit returns the func literal holding one ValueSpec\n339|// name: the index-paired value when every name carries its own,\n340|// the shared value when one serves all names, and nil for any\n341|// other shape or a non-literal value.\n342|func pairedFuncLit(value *ast.ValueSpec, index int) *ast.FuncLit {\n343|\tvar candidate ast.Expr\n344|\tswitch {\n345|\tcase len(value.Values) == len(value.Names) && index < len(value.Values):\n346|\t\tcandidate = value.Values[index]\n347|\tcase len(value.Values) == 1:\n348|\t\tcandidate = value.Values[0]\n349|\tdefault:\n350|\t\treturn nil\n351|\t}\n352|\tliteral, ok := candidate.(*ast.FuncLit)\n353|\tif !ok {\n354|\t\treturn nil\n355|\t}\n356|\treturn literal\n357|}\n358|\n359|// scopeRange is one named scope constructor calls attribute to:\n360|// a function declaration or a package-level variable holding a\n361|// func literal.\n362|type scopeRange struct {\n363|\tname       string\n364|\tstart, end token.Pos\n365|}\n366|\n367|// collectFileArms derives every arm in one production file from a\n368|// single parse, so scope containment compares positions within\n369|// one file set: constructor calls attribute to their innermost\n370|// enclosing scope by source range, frameFault literals derive\n371|// frame arms, and any constructor identifier outside call-fun\n372|// and definition position is an alias and fails the file.\n373|func collectFileArms(fileSet *token.FileSet, syntax *ast.File, constructors map[string]bool, arms map[string]struct{}) error {\n374|\tvar scopes []scopeRange\n375|\ttype pendingCall struct {\n376|\t\tname     string\n377|\t\tcall     *ast.CallExpr\n378|\t\tposition token.Pos\n379|\t}\n380|\tvar calls []pendingCall\n381|\tvar frames []*ast.CompositeLit\n382|\ttype identUse struct {\n383|\t\tidentifier *ast.Ident\n384|\t\tparent     ast.Node\n385|\t}\n386|\tvar uses []identUse\n387|\tvar stack []ast.Node\n388|\tast.Inspect(syntax, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n389|\t\tif node == nil {\n390|\t\t\tstack = stack[:len(stack)-1]\n391|\t\t\treturn true\n392|\t\t}\n393|\t\tvar parent ast.Node\n394|\t\tif len(stack) > 0 {\n395|\t\t\tparent = stack[len(stack)-1]\n396|\t\t}\n397|\t\tswitch node := node.(type) {\n398|\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl:\n399|\t\t\tscopes = append(scopes, scopeRange{name: node.Name.Name, start: node.Pos(), end: node.End()})\n400|\t\tcase *ast.GenDecl:\n401|\t\t\tfor _, specification := range node.Specs {\n402|\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := specification.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n403|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n404|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n405|\t\t\t\t}\n406|\t\t\t\tfor index, name := range value.Names {\n407|\t\t\t\t\tif index < len(value.Values) {\n408|\t\t\t\t\t\tif literal, ok := value.Values[index].(*ast.FuncLit); ok {\n409|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tscopes = append(scopes, scopeRange{name: \"var:\" + name.Name, start: literal.Pos(), end: literal.End()})\n410|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n411|\t\t\t\t\t}\n412|\t\t\t\t}\n413|\t\t\t}\n414|\t\tcase *ast.Ident:\n415|\t\t\tif constructors[node.Name] {\n416|\t\t\t\tuses = append(uses, identUse{identifier: node, parent: parent})\n417|\t\t\t}\n418|\t\tcase *ast.CallExpr:\n419|\t\t\tif fun, ok := node.Fun.(*ast.Ident); ok && constructors[fun.Name] {\n420|\t\t\t\tcalls = append(calls, pendingCall{name: fun.Name, call: node, position: node.Pos()})\n421|\t\t\t}\n422|\t\tcase *ast.CompositeLit:\n423|\t\t\tif identifier, ok := node.Type.(*ast.Ident); ok && identifier.Name == \"frameFault\" {\n424|\t\t\t\tframes = append(frames, node)\n425|\t\t\t}\n426|\t\t}\n427|\t\tstack = append(stack, node)\n428|\t\treturn true\n429|\t})\n430|\tfor _, use := range uses {\n431|\t\tif call, ok := use.parent.(*ast.CallExpr); ok {\n432|\t\t\tif fun, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.Ident); ok && fun == use.identifier {\n433|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n434|\t\t\t}\n435|\t\t}\n436|\t\tif specification, ok := use.parent.(*ast.ValueSpec); ok {\n437|\t\t\tdefined := false\n438|\t\t\tfor _, name := range specification.Names {\n439|\t\t\t\tif name == use.identifier {\n440|\t\t\t\t\tdefined = true\n441|\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n442|\t\t\t\t}\n443|\t\t\t}\n444|\t\t\tif defined {\n445|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n446|\t\t\t}\n447|\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"constructor alias of %s buries every arm it builds at %s\", use.identifier.Name, fileSet.Position(use.identifier.Pos()))\n448|\t\t}\n449|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"constructor alias or indirect use of %s at %s\", use.identifier.Name, fileSet.Position(use.identifier.Pos()))\n450|\t}\n451|\tenclosing := func(position token.Pos) string {\n452|\t\tbest := \"package\"\n453|\t\tvar bestStart token.Pos\n454|\t\tinitialized := false\n455|\t\tfor _, scope := range scopes {\n456|\t\t\tif scope.start <= position && position <= scope.end {\n457|\t\t\t\tif !initialized || scope.start >= bestStart {\n458|\t\t\t\t\tbest, bestStart, initialized = scope.name, scope.start, true\n459|\t\t\t\t}\n460|\t\t\t}\n461|\t\t}\n462|\t\treturn best\n463|\t}\n464|\tfor _, call := range calls {\n465|\t\tarm, err := callArm(call.name, call.call, enclosing(call.position))\n466|\t\tif err != nil {\n467|\t\t\treturn err\n468|\t\t}\n469|\t\tarms[arm] = struct{}{}\n470|\t}\n471|\tfor _, frame := range frames {\n472|\t\tdetail, err := frameDetail(frame)\n473|\t\tif err != nil {\n474|\t\t\treturn err\n475|\t\t}\n476|\t\tarms[\"frame|\"+detail] = struct{}{}\n477|\t}\n478|\treturn nil\n479|}\n480|\n481|// callArm derives one constructor arm: a string-literal first\n482|// argument is the detail; a literal-plus-fault.detail binary is a\n483|// conduit keyed by function and prefix; anything else is an\n484|// expr obligation keyed by function.\n485|func callArm(constructor string, call *ast.CallExpr, function string) (string, error) {\n486|\tif len(call.Args) == 0 {\n487|\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"constructor %s called with no arguments in %s\", constructor, function)\n488|\t}\n489|\tswitch first := call.Args[0].(type) {\n490|\tcase *ast.BasicLit:\n491|\t\tif first.Kind != token.STRING {\n492|\t\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"constructor %s first argument is not a string in %s\", constructor, function)\n493|\t\t}\n494|\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(first.Value)\n495|\t\tif err != nil {\n496|\t\t\treturn \"\", err\n497|\t\t}\n498|\t\treturn \"ctor|\" + constructor + \"|\" + detail, nil\n499|\tcase *ast.BinaryExpr:\n500|\t\tprefix, ok := first.X.(*ast.BasicLit)\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
