{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c971","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07476-3862-7671-a25f-75740245e24f"},"sequence":787,"recorded_at":1780531400001569,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"1306ed5a-6b54-4fd3-9851-7d107a5a6821"},"task_id":"1306ed5a-6b54-4fd3-9851-7d107a5a6821","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"1306ed5a-6b54-4fd3-9851-7d107a5a6821","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-13-1\",\n  \"command\": \"tail -n 60 LOGBOOK.md; echo \\\"=== git log worktree ===\\\"; git log --oneline -5 -- internal/sessadapter/ | head; echo \\\"=== status ===\\\"; git status --short | head -n 20\",\n  \"description\": \"Check logbook tail and git state\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"- FIX (F4): attach expiry pinned from both sides — admitted one second before `expires`, refused exactly at it. `!now.Before(expires)` → `now.After(expires)` now fails the suite.\\n- BOUNDS (carried forward, not dropped): the inventory kills every arm-deleting mutant by construction, so post-leaf-3 mutation scores are NOT comparable to leaf 2's 91/95 — stated in the inventory file's Stated bounds block and here. Attribution drift survives via the entry+code fallback — live example `CheckTransition`'s dead `\\\"operation vocabulary\\\"` arm resolving through `ParseOperation`'s test — also stated there. Declined closure: P13 (empty-ID `ProjectToLegacy` still refuses, different wire code). P11 (legacy escape name) is no longer declined: C20 (`legacyForward` gains `\\\"screen\\\"`) is killed by `TestLegacyReverseProjectionExistsOnlyForThePair`, so the closed-set property is pinned.\\n- EVIDENCE: A1/A2/P8/P16/P20 replayed, each red with exit 1, tree restored byte-identical (shasum). Full gates re-run below.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (derivation + bounds), `conformance_test.go` (F2–F4); `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry, 89.9% correction). No production change, no table change, README sentence stands as written now that the derivation covers it.\\n- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14/14), `-race` on terminalbackend exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (`acceptance_cases=76`, section coverage unchanged). Package coverage 90.0% statements measured on this rework tree (test-only additions vs the rev-1 tree the reviewer measured at 89.9%). Rework left uncommitted in the working tree per the brief (board checkpoints, no commit).\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1snnef round-2 rework: three sampled closures of one family, closed by derivation\\n- FINDING (G2): `TestPlainErrorsLiveOnlyInTheirTwoFunctions` walked FuncDecl bodies only — the exact walk `deriveRefusalArms` was extended past in round 1, 200 lines above in the same file. Identical `errors.New` text was red in a FuncDecl and green in a package-level var (W5b), `fmt.Errorf` likewise (W9b), var func literal likewise (W16).\\n- FIX (G2): the sibling walk gained the same GenDecl/ValueSpec loop (shared `isPlainErrorConstruction` helper, receiver-qualified method names). Twin-hunt over the story boundary (`internal/terminalbackend` AST walks): `deriveRefusalArms` already extended, `rejectConstructorAliases` inspects whole files, `productionCodeSymbols` walks package-level const GenDecls by construction, `testBodies`/`predicateCodes` are func-scoped by convention and fail closed, the platform funnel is function-scoped by design. No other twin. Bonus kill: an unused package-level plain-error var (W18 shape) is now red too — its initializer runs at package init, so the construction is real.\\n- FIX (G1): `TestCheckStatusResultEnforcesLookupRules` now derives the complement — every state the production parser admits (`derivedParserVocabulary` over the switch-case list) outside parked/active is refused with attach evidenced; parked/active admitted. C13/C26/C27/C28/C29 each red, C30 still red.\\n- FIX (G3): new internal `TestReplicationMembersAreExactlyTheClosedTable` pins the live `replicationMembers` map in both directions plus the size (64 members). C40c (add) and C40-init-injection red there; C40b/C40d red there and at the entry. External test comment restated to its half (want subset production) with the reverse cited.\\n- FIX (G4): new `TestDerivedVocabulariesAreExactlyTheAdmittedSets` derives all four parser vocabularies (states, operations, effects, transports) from switch-case lists resolved through string consts, both directions plus size, and pins `conformanceOperations` to the derived operation set — the \\\"pinned by\\\" citation now holds. Refused samples restated as sampling bounds over the unbounded string domain and extended with the reviewer's exact survivor strings (`detached`, `detach`, `input_reopened`, `ssh_tunnel`), each now behaviorally refused.\\n- BOUNDS (recorded, not closed): W11 (DigestFile allowlist is function-wide, no detail pin), W13 (bespoke error types outside both spellings), mismatchf format-verb interpolation (derivation now fatals on any constructor call without exactly one string-literal argument — zero such sites today; vet catches non-constant formats). P11 stale bound dropped (C20 killed); P13 declined closure stands.\\n- TOOLING: round-3 runner (`.temp/TASK-260830-1snnef-r2/probe.py` family successor `.temp/TASK-260830-1snnef-r3/probe3.py`) snapshots and hash-verifies every touched file regardless of extension, with a JSON-restore self-test and a porcelain+fingerprint tree-identity check — a T01-shaped JSON mutation can no longer contaminate the tree.\\n- EVIDENCE: 21/21 replayed red, 0 survived, 0 anchor-missing (G1x6 incl. control, G2x5 incl. control and unused-var, G3x4 incl. init injection and both reclassifications, G4x5 incl. control, F2 guard). Tree verified identical before/after (porcelain + watched hashes).\\n- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/conformance_test.go` (G1/G3-comment/G4), `internal_pin_test.go` (G3 pin), `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (G2 twin + single-arg assertion + bounds), `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry + P11 correction). No production change, no arm-table change, 193/193 undisturbed.\\n- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14/14), `-race` on terminalbackend exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (`acceptance_cases=76`, `clauses_discharged=17/403`). Package coverage 90.0% statements. Rework left uncommitted in the working tree per the brief (board checkpoints, no commit).\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1snnef round-3 rework: unpinned legacyForward closed by a white-box pin, plus a correction\\n- CORRECTION: the round-1 and round-2 entries above claim C20 (`legacyForward` gains `\\\"screen\\\"`) is killed by `TestLegacyReverseProjectionExistsOnlyForThePair` and drop the P11 bound on that basis. That claim is false, and the error is the reviewer's (round-2 verdict), not the producer's — the rework followed the verdict. C20 lands on `BuiltinTmux` while `ProjectToLegacy` iterates a map, so the kill was a coin flip over iteration order: 5 red and 7 green across 12 runs of the reviewer's own probe. A single red on a map-iteration mutant proves nothing. LESSON, applied to every mutant below: a mutant over map iteration (or anything else iterating a map, e.g. `ProjectToLegacy`) is run repeatedly before its verdict is believed.\\n- FIX (H1, blocking): new white-box `TestLegacyForwardIsExactlyTheImmutablePair` (`internal_pin_test.go`) holds the live `legacyForward` map to exactly `{tmux, conpty}` in both directions plus the size — the `replicationMembers` idiom from this same CR — and additionally pins injectivity (distinct canonical values), which `ProjectToLegacy`'s documented determinism rested on unenforced. The black-box forward comment is restated to its half (sampling bound, not closure) with the reverse cited, and the reviewer's escape strings join the refused samples (`TranslateLegacyBackend(\\\"screen\\\")`, `ProjectToLegacy(\\\"vendor.screen\\\")`).\\n- FIX (H2, bound, closed cheaply): new `rejectPlainErrorAliases` fails the suite on any `errors.New`/`fmt.Errorf`-kin reference outside direct-call position, in every function including the two allowlisted ones (an alias inside `validatePlatforms` would bypass the funneled detail pin). Stated bounds and the allowlist test comment record the closure. Bespoke error types outside both spellings remain the disclosed bound.\\n- EVIDENCE: L3 (`\\\"screen\\\": \\\"vendor.screen\\\"`) 12/12 red, C20 (`\\\"screen\\\": BuiltinTmux`) 12/12 red, each over `-run TestLegacy|TestHistorical`; the new pin alone red on C20 with the size message (`holds 3 names, want exactly 2`); H2 alias (`var newPlain = errors.New` + call from a FuncDecl) 3/3 red on `TestPlainErrors`. Tree verified identical before/after (file-content compare + restore assert).\\n- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/internal_pin_test.go` (H1 pin), `conformance_test.go` (H1 comment + 2 samples), `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (H2 alias gate + bounds), `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry). No production change, no arm-table change, 193/193 undisturbed.\\n- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14/14), `-race` on terminalbackend exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (`acceptance_cases=76`, `clauses_discharged=17/403`). Rework left uncommitted in the working tree per the brief (board checkpoints, no commit).\\n\\n### 2321 — A local copy of a shared gate needs a pin, not a comment; a registry that only counts itself cannot see new code\\n- ROOT CAUSE (B3): `provhost.decodeStrictObject` re-implemented strict decoding without the shared `canonicaljson` surrogate rule, and Go's `encoding/json` replaces a lone `\\\\ud800` escape with U+FFFD silently — so Section 1.6 wire bodies carrying lone surrogates were admitted. Same class as the sibling story's decoder gap.\\n- FIX: local `hasLoneSurrogateEscape` gate in `internal/provhost/surrogate.go` (local copy because `canonicaljson` is frozen across both unlanded stories), called first from `decodeStrictObject`; one `\\\\ud800` fixture per production entry plus `TestSurrogateGateAgreesWithCanonicalJSON`, a 13-vector pin driving both the local gate and `canonicaljson.Canonicalize` so the copies cannot drift.\\n- ANOMALY: the first gate version used `switch` and reddened `TestAllProductionSwitchesAreClassified` — the package census bans switches as membership-gate hiding spots. Rewritten with if/else, identical verdicts, green. A gate's own residue rules apply to the fix too.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (B4): `tracecheck` verifies registry -> code only, so ~3,700 lines of `internal/provider` + `internal/provhost` landed with the gate green under gap prose asserting \\\"no provider manifest is implemented anywhere\\\". The census enumerates what registered itself.\\n- FIX: 4 acceptance cases + 4 section bindings (7.1, 7.6, 7.7, 8), 4 gap rewrites (5.5, 7.2, 7.3, 7.5), re-pinned hash; report now bindings=53 unevidenced=45 clauses 17/428. Reverse scan (every `internal/*` package owned or explicitly excluded) recorded as open work, not implemented here.\\n- DECISION (A2/A3/A4, recorded in code): CheckIdentity duplication is deliberate (different error surface, shared package frozen); Provider Protocol 3.0.0 is a stated non-owner bound, not a defect; provider's cause-appending errors must be rebuilt, not quoted, at the future cmd/ax lift (`refuseCausalLeak`).\\n- SCOPE: `internal/provhost/surrogate*.go`, `protocol.go`, refusal inventory (floor 162->164), `profile_test.go` (cross-plane set test), `identity.go`/`doc.go` bounds, `internal/provider/doc.go` composition contract, ownership registry + pin + report/golden/README figures.\\n- STATUS: Resolved. `go test ./...` and `-cover` green, vet + GOOS=windows vet + gofmt clean, admit-all and narrowing mutants red as required. TASK-260830-32jeti round-4, handed to review.\\n\\n### 1244 — A deadline borrowed from pipe ownership is not a deadline; a shared hand list is not a pin\\n- ROOT CAUSE (F1): the `os.Pipe` rewrite in `internal/provhost/runner.go` fixed the Wait-closes-StdoutPipe race but removed the only thing that unblocked the post-Wait drain. `exec.WaitDelay` closes pipes exec itself owns; with caller-supplied `*os.File` pipes nothing closes them, so `readCapped` waits for EOF until every writer is gone and a setsid-detached grandchild holds `Host.Call` open for its whole lifetime (measured 20.3-20.7s against sleep 20, frame accepted with err=nil).\\n- FIX: the waiter owns the bound now — `command.Wait()` runs in a goroutine under `select` on the call context, both drains collect through `collectDrains` under the same context, and closing the read ends fails blocked drains at once. A `Process.Kill` backstop covers a self-detached direct child, which the group-aimed `Cancel` misses. The round-6 EPIPE rule is untouched: with the wait reaped and stdout holding a frame, the frame still governs.\\n- ANOMALY: the first regression probe passed vacuously in 0.79s — python3 cold start under load can exceed the 400ms deadline kill, so no grandchild ever existed to hold the pipe. A hang test whose fixture loses a startup race proves nothing. Rebuilt on perl (millisecond start) with the kill seconds away; 3/3 red at the sleeper lifetime before the fix, green at the deadline after.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (F2): the 13-vector corpus was literal-versus-literal — both implementations matched the same hand list, so a narrowed low-surrogate ceiling (SG1, 1023 admitted) and a narrowed uppercase hex range (SG5, 473 admitted) survived 6/6. Raw WTF-8 (`\\\\xed\\\\xa0\\\\x80`) arrived through an encoding the escape scanner never sees and became U+FFFD silently.\\n- FIX: `decodeStrictObject` refuses non-UTF-8 first (mirroring `canonicaljson.decodeStrict` order), and the corpus is replaced by a 239,630-vector derived sweep — full BMP x hex case, surrogate x 16 case mixes, high x boundary/non-low seconds, sampled positions plus all-surrogate member names, full BMP raw (WTF-8 form for surrogates), malformed patterns, astral samples — every verdict judged by the independent implementation. SG1 diverges on 19,482 vectors, SG5 on 4,411; gate removal reddens the identity row with err=nil and the sweep on 2,059.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (F3): `checkResponseMembers` ran before the version gate, so only a v2-shaped 3.x envelope reached `incompatible_protocol`; the tree's own pinned 7.2 quote scopes that member rule to major 2. Fixed the ordering, not the doc: a `foreignMajor` peek (protocol identity plus readable foreign version, trusts nothing, refuses nothing) skips the v2 `ok`/member rules so the single existing mismatch site decides. No new refusal arm; floor untouched by F3.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/provhost/runner.go`, `protocol.go`, `surrogate*.go`, `identity.go` + comment corrections, `runner_test.go`, `protocol_test.go`, `identity_test.go`, refusal inventory (floor 164->166: one UTF-8 frame arm plus its status-body expansion, each witnessed).\\n- STATUS: Resolved. Build, vet, GOOS=windows vet, gofmt clean; `go test ./...` 15/15 green; provhost `-race` green; provhost 85.8%, provider 97.0%. TASK-260830-32jeti round-8, handed to review.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-32jeti: two green branches, one red combination — syscall.Mkfifo under GOOS=windows vet\\n- FINDING: the new CI step `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` failed on the merged tree with `terminalbackend_test.go:972:20: undefined: syscall.Mkfifo` — the only failure across all 16 packages. Invisible on both parents by construction: the story branch added the gate before the package existed (nothing to compile, exit 0), and trunk added the `syscall.Mkfifo` FIFO case without the gate (never compiled under Windows). Each branch was green on its own; only the combination is red. A per-branch gate that never meets the code it must check proves nothing about the merge.\\n- FIX: moved only the FIFO case out of `TestDigestFile` into `TestDigestFileRefusesFIFO` in new `internal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend_unix_test.go`, following the `internal/localstore/projection_unix_test.go` pattern. Correction worth recording: the `_unix` filename suffix alone constrains nothing (`unix` is a build tag, not a GOOS value, so the suffix form matches no `_GOOS` pattern) — the first attempt with suffix-only still failed windows vet, and the explicit `//go:build unix` line is what excludes Windows. The shared test file drops the `syscall` import and keeps a pointer comment; no other Go file touched.\\n- EVIDENCE: `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./... -count=1` 16/16 green with `TestDigestFileRefusesFIFO` observed PASS on linux (a moved test that stops executing is not a fix), `tracecheck` exit 0. TASK-260830-32jeti, handed to review.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0: sessadapter closed-vocabulary census derived from the pinned document, vocab gates looped, acceptance cases registered\\n- FIX: `census_test.go` used `specdoc` without deriving from it (vet failure on the unused import). Added `TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec` (20 closed bodies: every Required list in document order plus the Members map as a set, with the success/failure envelopes derived by the spec's own first-four-fields rule, the manifest from its table's first-column spans, and the doctor result from the operation table) and `TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec` (16 vocabularies pinned to their spec unions; operation/capability registries in order, value sets as sets).\\n- FINDINGS (all verified against the raw document, each would have been a silent wrong-source derivation): the request envelope sentence exists three times (7.5-style, 7.8, 7.9) and the capability-value sentence twice (Provider Probe 7.4 vs Session Adapter Probe 7.8) — selection is by a structural fragment only the Session Adapter sentence carries, and the parse still covers the whole sentence; member sentences contain digit-period-digit abbreviations (`Section 7.5`, `Structured Error 1.1`), so the sentence scanner skips those; unions use three pipe encodings (`\\\\|` in the operation table, raw `|` in prose, `&#124;` in the manifest table); the manifest table pairs members per row (`schema`/`schema_version` etc.), so the first cell contributes every bare snake_case span; the `probe` row name recurs in four tables, so row unions are windowed to the 7.8 registry table; fidelity profiles come from the `projection-plan` operation row (4 values — the 13.14 `Profiles are` sentence lists 5 including `archive_only`, which is a strategy there, never a profile).\\n- REFACTOR (production-first, same `var` + `validX` loop idiom the package already uses): `capabilityStatuses`/`validCapabilityStatus` (probe.go), `readPurposes`/`validReadPurpose` and `findingSeverities`/`validFindingSeverity` (context.go), `tupleArchitectures`/`validTupleArchitecture` (tuple.go); the four inline-literal checks now loop the tables. Roles, directions, candidate kinds, and platforms derive from the existing `Role`/`Direction`/`CandidateKind`/`scalar.Platform` consts with no production change (tuple platforms delegate to `scalar.ParsePlatform`).\\n- TEST: new `TestDecodeProbeClosedRules/bad_status` — no behavioral test refused a fifth status, so a `return true` mutant of `validCapabilityStatus` survived the suite with the static census green. The mutant is now killed by the entry point (`DecodeProbe`).\\n- EVIDENCE (executed mutants, `/tmp/sessadapter-mutants.sh`, tree verified identical before/after): M1 `capabilityStatuses`+`bogus` killed by `TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec`; M2 `findingSeverities`+`fatal` killed by `TestDecodeFindingRules/bad_severity`; M3 `requestMembers`+`zzz` killed by `TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec/request_envelope`; M4 `validCapabilityStatus`→`return true` (all searched-for tokens preserved) leaves the static census green and is killed by the behavioral suite (`TestDecodeProbeClosedRules/bad_status`); M5 unregistered vocabulary-shaped `var` killed by `TestClosedVocabularyTablesAreRegistered`. 8/8 as required, 0 survived.\\n- TRACEABILITY: 7 acceptance cases appended (`session-adapter-discovery/-manifest/-probe/-operations/-limits/-idempotency/-tuple-gates`, each bound to one production declaration and its named positive/refusal tests), digest re-pinned to `78d9bc9b...`, count pins 81->88, README ownership paragraph 81->88 plus a sessadapter disclosure paragraph that keeps the Section 7.8 clause-level binding `unevidenced` (no clause enumerated — no clause-level claim made).\\n- NOTE (pre-existing, not touched): README still says \\\"One admitted binding out of forty-nine\\\" while `tracecheck` measures `bindings=53` — stale since before this task (first run here already showed 53). Flagged for the review rather than fixed in passing.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/sessadapter/{census_test,probe,context,tuple}.go` + `probe_test.go` (bad status), `internal/traceability/{ownership.v0.5.0.json,traceability.go,traceability_test.go,cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go}`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry). Work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n=== git log worktree ===\\n=== status ===\\n M LOGBOOK.md\\n M README.md\\n M internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go\\n M internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json\\n M internal/traceability/traceability.go\\n M internal/traceability/traceability_test.go\\n?? internal/sessadapter/\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 20378,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 5095,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
