{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c975","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07476-3862-7671-a25f-75740245e24f"},"sequence":789,"recorded_at":1780531400001573,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a"},"call_id":"call_01a074784a357812bdd04660f4c4efdc","text":"Read text file `internal/sessadapter/operations_test.go`.\n1|package sessadapter\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"encoding/json\"\n5|\t\"fmt\"\n6|\t\"strings\"\n7|\t\"testing\"\n8|)\n9|\n10|// Request builders: one valid request body per operation. Contexts\n11|// name the real fixture manifest digest so bodies bind to sealed\n12|// bindings downstream.\n13|\n14|func requestContext(t *testing.T, manifestDigest string) (string, CallContext) {\n15|\tt.Helper()\n16|\tskeleton := fmt.Sprintf(`{\"context\":%s,\"authority\":%s,\"workspace_filter\":null,\"limit\":50,\"cursor\":null,\"extensions\":{}}`,\n17|\t\tcontextSkeleton(manifestDigest, \"sha256:\"+strings.Repeat(\"0\", 64)), fixtureReadAuthorityJSON())\n18|\tdigest, err := RequestDigestFor([]byte(skeleton))\n19|\tif err != nil {\n20|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"RequestDigestFor: %v\", err)\n21|\t}\n22|\tbody := fmt.Sprintf(`{\"context\":%s,\"authority\":%s,\"workspace_filter\":null,\"limit\":50,\"cursor\":null,\"extensions\":{}}`,\n23|\t\tcontextSkeleton(manifestDigest, digest.String()), fixtureReadAuthorityJSON())\n24|\tcontext, err := CheckRequestBody(OpDiscover, []byte(body))\n25|\tif err != nil {\n26|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"requestContext: %v\", err)\n27|\t}\n28|\treturn contextSkeleton(manifestDigest, digest.String()), context\n29|}\n30|\n31|func contextSkeleton(manifestDigest, requestDigest string) string {\n32|\treturn fmt.Sprintf(`{\"operation_id\":%q,\"provider_id\":%q,\"environment\":%s,\"session_adapter_manifest_digest\":%q,\"executable_sha256\":%q,\"request_digest\":%q,\"extensions\":{}}`,\n33|\t\tfixtureOperationID, fixtureProviderID, fixtureTupleJSON(), manifestDigest, fixtureExecutableDigest, requestDigest)\n34|}\n35|\n36|// fixtureRequestBody builds one valid request body per operation.\n37|// The manifest digest binds every context to the fixture manifest.\n38|func fixtureRequestBody(t *testing.T, operation Operation, manifestDigest string) []byte {\n39|\tt.Helper()\n40|\tauthority := fixtureReadAuthorityJSON()\n41|\tsource := `{\"native_session_id\":\"sess-1\",\"logical_workspace_id\":null,\"opaque_source_ref\":null}`\n42|\tboundary := `{}`\n43|\tcontextJSON, _ := requestContext(t, manifestDigest)\n44|\tctx := `\"context\":` + contextJSON\n45|\tswitch operation {\n46|\tcase OpManifest:\n47|\t\treturn []byte(`{}`)\n48|\tcase OpProbe:\n49|\t\treturn []byte(`{\"expected_provider_id\":` + quote(fixtureProviderID) + `,\"expected_candidate_kind\":\"builtin\",\"extensions\":{}}`)\n50|\tcase OpDiscover:\n51|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"authority\":` + authority + `,\"workspace_filter\":null,\"limit\":50,\"cursor\":null,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n52|\tcase OpInspect:\n53|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"authority\":` + authority + `,\"source\":` + source + `,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n54|\tcase OpSnapshotProof:\n55|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"authority\":` + authority + `,\"source\":` + source + `,\"expected_source_store_generation\":\"gen-7\",\"allow_provider_quiescence\":false,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n56|\tcase OpCapturePlan:\n57|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"authority\":` + authority + `,\"source\":` + source + `,\"capture_boundary\":` + boundary + `,\"plan_sink\":` + fixtureFreshSinkJSON(\"capture_plan\") + `,\"max_items\":10,\"max_total_bytes\":1000,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n58|\tcase OpCapture:\n59|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"source_authority\":` + authority + `,\"sink\":` + fixtureFreshSinkJSON(\"raw_source\") + `,\"source\":` + source + `,\"capture_boundary\":` + boundary + `,\"capture_plan_digest\":` + quote(fixturePlanDigest) + `,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n60|\tcase OpNormalize:\n61|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"capture_manifest_id\":` + quote(fixtureCaptureDigest) + `,\"raw_objects\":` + fixtureFreshSinkJSON(\"raw_source\") + `,\"canonical_sink\":` + fixtureFreshSinkJSON(\"canonical_source\") + `,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n62|\tcase OpProjectionPlan:\n63|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"capture_manifest_id\":` + quote(fixtureCaptureDigest) + `,\"canonical_session_id\":` + quote(fixtureSessionDigest) + `,\"canonical_event_ids\":[],\"source_objects\":` + fixtureFreshSinkJSON(\"canonical_source\") + `,\"plan_sink\":` + fixtureFreshSinkJSON(\"projection_plan\") + `,\"target_environment\":` + fixtureTupleJSON() + `,\"expected_target_native_session_id\":\"target-1\",\"fidelity_profile\":\"maximal_safe\",\"required_dispositions\":{\"user_message\":[\"exact\"]},\"forbid_reasons\":[],\"resource_limits\":{\"max_objects\":10,\"max_total_bytes\":1000,\"max_single_object_bytes\":100,\"max_events\":5,\"max_target_resources\":5},\"extensions\":{}}`)\n64|\tcase OpProject:\n65|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"projection_plan_id\":` + quote(fixturePlanDigest) + `,\"capture_manifest_id\":` + quote(fixtureCaptureDigest) + `,\"canonical_session_id\":` + quote(fixtureSessionDigest) + `,\"source_objects\":` + fixtureFreshSinkJSON(\"canonical_source\") + `,\"target_sink\":` + fixtureFreshSinkJSON(\"projected_target\") + `,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n66|\tcase OpReadBack:\n67|\t\tstaged := mutateAuthority(t, authority, \"target_staged\")\n68|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"authority\":` + staged + `,\"expected_target_native_session_id\":\"target-1\",\"projection_plan_id\":` + quote(fixturePlanDigest) + `,\"projected_object_manifest_id\":` + quote(fixtureProjectedDigest) + `,\"evidence_sink\":` + fixtureFreshSinkJSON(\"read_back_evidence\") + `,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n69|\tcase OpValidate:\n70|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"mode\":\"staged\",\"capture_manifest_id\":` + quote(fixtureCaptureDigest) + `,\"canonical_session_id\":` + quote(fixtureSessionDigest) + `,\"projection_plan_id\":` + quote(fixturePlanDigest) + `,\"projected_object_manifest_id\":` + quote(fixtureProjectedDigest) + `,\"read_back_evidence_manifest_id\":` + quote(fixtureReadBackDigest) + `,\"expected_target_native_session_id\":\"target-1\",\"extensions\":{}}`)\n71|\tcase OpResumePlan:\n72|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"authority\":` + authority + `,\"expected_target_native_session_id\":\"target-1\",\"projection_plan_id\":` + quote(fixturePlanDigest) + `,\"target_checkpoint_id\":null,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n73|\tcase OpDoctor:\n74|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"direction\":\"source_read\",\"tuple_registry_digest\":` + quote(fixtureRegistryDigest) + `,\"refresh_requested\":false,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n75|\tdefault:\n76|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"no request fixture for %q\", operation)\n77|\t\treturn nil\n78|\t}\n79|}\n80|\n81|func quote(value string) string {\n82|\treturn `\"` + value + `\"`\n83|}\n84|\n85|// mutateAuthority rebuilds the authority fixture with a purpose.\n86|func mutateAuthority(t *testing.T, authority, purpose string) string {\n87|\tt.Helper()\n88|\tvar members map[string]json.RawMessage\n89|\tif err := json.Unmarshal([]byte(authority), &members); err != nil {\n90|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"mutateAuthority: %v\", err)\n91|\t}\n92|\tmembers[\"purpose\"] = json.RawMessage(`\"` + purpose + `\"`)\n93|\trebuilt, err := json.Marshal(members)\n94|\tif err != nil {\n95|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"mutateAuthority: %v\", err)\n96|\t}\n97|\treturn string(rebuilt)\n98|}\n99|\n100|// fixtureSuccessBody builds one valid success body per operation\n101|// over the request context bytes.\n102|func fixtureSuccessBody(t *testing.T, operation Operation, contextJSON string, manifestDigest string) []byte {\n103|\tt.Helper()\n104|\tctx := `\"context\":` + contextJSON\n105|\tswitch operation {\n106|\tcase OpDiscover:\n107|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"sources\":[],\"next_cursor\":null,\"partial\":false,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n108|\tcase OpInspect:\n109|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"source\":{},\"source_identity\":{},\"source_store_generation\":\"gen-7\",\"environment\":` + fixtureTupleJSON() + `,\"ambiguities\":[],\"extensions\":{}}`)\n110|\tcase OpSnapshotProof:\n111|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"proof\":{},\"provider_quiescence_requested\":false,\"provider_quiescence_observed\":false,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n112|\tcase OpCapturePlan:\n113|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"source_identity\":{},\"source_store_generation\":\"gen-7\",\"capture_plan_candidate_id\":` + quote(fixturePlanDigest) + `,\"candidate_count\":0,\"excluded_classes\":[],\"capture_plan_digest\":` + quote(fixturePlanDigest) + `,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n114|\tcase OpCapture:\n115|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"capture_plan_digest\":` + quote(fixturePlanDigest) + `,\"source_store_generation\":\"gen-7\",\"capture_result_candidate_id\":` + quote(fixtureDigest(\"result\")) + `,\"source_raw_object_manifest_candidate_id\":` + quote(fixtureDigest(\"raw-manifest\")) + `,\"item_count\":0,\"pre_capture_digest\":` + quote(fixtureDigest(\"pre\")) + `,\"post_capture_digest\":` + quote(fixtureDigest(\"post\")) + `,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n116|\tcase OpNormalize:\n117|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"capture_manifest_id\":` + quote(fixtureCaptureDigest) + `,\"canonical_session_candidate_id\":` + quote(fixtureSessionDigest) + `,\"canonical_event_candidate_ids\":[],\"raw_reference_ids\":[],\"extensions\":{}}`)\n118|\tcase OpProjectionPlan:\n119|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"projection_plan_candidate_id\":` + quote(fixturePlanDigest) + `,\"required_source_object_ids\":[],\"predicted_counts\":{},\"findings\":[],\"extensions\":{}}`)\n120|\tcase OpProject:\n121|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"projection_plan_id\":` + quote(fixturePlanDigest) + `,\"projected_object_manifest_candidate_id\":` + quote(fixtureProjectedDigest) + `,\"created_resource_keys\":[],\"actual_counts\":{},\"extensions\":{}}`)\n122|\tcase OpReadBack:\n123|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"observed_target_native_session_id\":\"target-1\",\"projection_plan_id\":` + quote(fixturePlanDigest) + `,\"observed_environment\":` + fixtureTupleJSON() + `,\"parsed_event_count\":0,\"parsed_head_ids\":[],\"workspace_binding\":{},\"structural_digest\":` + quote(fixtureStructuralDigest) + `,\"read_back_evidence_manifest_candidate_id\":` + quote(fixtureReadBackDigest) + `,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n124|\tcase OpValidate:\n125|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"mode\":\"staged\",\"valid\":true,\"structural_valid\":true,\"semantic_marker_valid\":true,\"identity_valid\":null,\"workspace_binding_valid\":null,\"resume_surface_valid\":null,\"findings\":[],\"evidence_digest\":` + quote(fixtureEvidenceDigest) + `,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n126|\tcase OpResumePlan:\n127|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"target_native_session_id\":\"target-1\",\"projection_plan_id\":` + quote(fixturePlanDigest) + `,\"argv\":[\"ax\",\"open\",\"target-1\"],\"cwd_relative\":\".\",\"environment_names\":[],\"opens_existing_identity\":true,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n128|\tcase OpDoctor:\n129|\t\treturn []byte(`{` + ctx + `,\"direction\":\"source_read\",\"registry_sequence\":9,\"registry_entry_status\":\"accepted\",\"findings\":[],\"healthy\":false,\"extensions\":{}}`)\n130|\tdefault:\n131|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"no success fixture for %q\", operation)\n132|\t\treturn nil\n133|\t}\n134|}\n135|\n136|// requestContextOf extracts the context bytes from a request body.\n137|func requestContextOf(t *testing.T, body []byte) string {\n138|\tt.Helper()\n139|\treturn string(rawMember(t, body, \"context\"))\n140|}\n141|\n142|// TestEveryOperationHasContractVectors drives every registry\n143|// operation through both production entry points with a valid\n144|// body: 14 of 14 request vectors and 11 of 11 success vectors\n145|// (manifest, probe, and doctor successes decode through their\n146|// dedicated decoders, covered by their own tests). An operation\n147|// with no vector fails here rather than passing silently.\n148|func TestEveryOperationHasContractVectors(t *testing.T) {\n149|\tmanifestDigest := fixtureManifestDigestText(t)\n150|\t_, context := requestContext(t, manifestDigest)\n151|\t_ = context\n152|\tdrivenRequests := 0\n153|\tdrivenSuccesses := 0\n154|\tfor _, name := range Operations() {\n155|\t\toperation := Operation(name)\n156|\t\trequest := fixtureRequestBody(t, operation, manifestDigest)\n157|\t\tdecoded, err := CheckRequestBody(operation, request)\n158|\t\tif err != nil {\n159|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CheckRequestBody(%q): %v\", operation, err)\n160|\t\t}\n161|\t\tdrivenRequests++\n162|\t\tif operation == OpManifest || operation == OpProbe || operation == OpDoctor {\n163|\t\t\tcontinue\n164|\t\t}\n165|\t\tfacts := SuccessFacts{Context: decoded, ValidateMode: \"staged\", ResumeTargetID: \"target-1\", DoctorDirection: DirectionSourceRead}\n166|\t\tif operation == OpValidate {\n167|\t\t\tfacts.ValidateMode = \"staged\"\n168|\t\t}\n169|\t\tsuccess := fixtureSuccessBody(t, operation, requestContextOf(t, request), manifestDigest)\n170|\t\tif err := CheckSuccessBody(operation, success, facts); err != nil {\n171|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CheckSuccessBody(%q): %v\", operation, err)\n172|\t\t}\n173|\t\tdrivenSuccesses++\n174|\t}\n175|\tif drivenRequests != 14 {\n176|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"request vectors = %d, want 14\", drivenRequests)\n177|\t}\n178|\tif drivenSuccesses != 11 {\n179|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"success vectors = %d, want 11\", drivenSuccesses)\n180|\t}\n181|\tt.Logf(\"contract vectors: %d/14 requests, %d/11 successes, 3 dedicated decoders\", drivenRequests, drivenSuccesses)\n182|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c977","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07476-3862-7671-a25f-75740245e24f"},"sequence":790,"recorded_at":1780531400001575,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a"},"call_id":"call_01a074784aea7e5180db52f88a87b16c","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-13-1\",\n  \"command\": \"tail -n 60 LOGBOOK.md; echo \\\"=== git log worktree ===\\\"; git log --oneline -5 -- internal/sessadapter/ | head; echo \\\"=== status ===\\\"; git status --short | head -n 20\",\n  \"description\": \"Check logbook tail and git state\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"- FIX (F4): attach expiry pinned from both sides — admitted one second before `expires`, refused exactly at it. `!now.Before(expires)` → `now.After(expires)` now fails the suite.\\n- BOUNDS (carried forward, not dropped): the inventory kills every arm-deleting mutant by construction, so post-leaf-3 mutation scores are NOT comparable to leaf 2's 91/95 — stated in the inventory file's Stated bounds block and here. Attribution drift survives via the entry+code fallback — live example `CheckTransition`'s dead `\\\"operation vocabulary\\\"` arm resolving through `ParseOperation`'s test — also stated there. Declined closure: P13 (empty-ID `ProjectToLegacy` still refuses, different wire code). P11 (legacy escape name) is no longer declined: C20 (`legacyForward` gains `\\\"screen\\\"`) is killed by `TestLegacyReverseProjectionExistsOnlyForThePair`, so the closed-set property is pinned.\\n- EVIDENCE: A1/A2/P8/P16/P20 replayed, each red with exit 1, tree restored byte-identical (shasum). Full gates re-run below.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (derivation + bounds), `conformance_test.go` (F2–F4); `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry, 89.9% correction). No production change, no table change, README sentence stands as written now that the derivation covers it.\\n- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14/14), `-race` on terminalbackend exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (`acceptance_cases=76`, section coverage unchanged). Package coverage 90.0% statements measured on this rework tree (test-only additions vs the rev-1 tree the reviewer measured at 89.9%). Rework left uncommitted in the working tree per the brief (board checkpoints, no commit).\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1snnef round-2 rework: three sampled closures of one family, closed by derivation\\n- FINDING (G2): `TestPlainErrorsLiveOnlyInTheirTwoFunctions` walked FuncDecl bodies only — the exact walk `deriveRefusalArms` was extended past in round 1, 200 lines above in the same file. Identical `errors.New` text was red in a FuncDecl and green in a package-level var (W5b), `fmt.Errorf` likewise (W9b), var func literal likewise (W16).\\n- FIX (G2): the sibling walk gained the same GenDecl/ValueSpec loop (shared `isPlainErrorConstruction` helper, receiver-qualified method names). Twin-hunt over the story boundary (`internal/terminalbackend` AST walks): `deriveRefusalArms` already extended, `rejectConstructorAliases` inspects whole files, `productionCodeSymbols` walks package-level const GenDecls by construction, `testBodies`/`predicateCodes` are func-scoped by convention and fail closed, the platform funnel is function-scoped by design. No other twin. Bonus kill: an unused package-level plain-error var (W18 shape) is now red too — its initializer runs at package init, so the construction is real.\\n- FIX (G1): `TestCheckStatusResultEnforcesLookupRules` now derives the complement — every state the production parser admits (`derivedParserVocabulary` over the switch-case list) outside parked/active is refused with attach evidenced; parked/active admitted. C13/C26/C27/C28/C29 each red, C30 still red.\\n- FIX (G3): new internal `TestReplicationMembersAreExactlyTheClosedTable` pins the live `replicationMembers` map in both directions plus the size (64 members). C40c (add) and C40-init-injection red there; C40b/C40d red there and at the entry. External test comment restated to its half (want subset production) with the reverse cited.\\n- FIX (G4): new `TestDerivedVocabulariesAreExactlyTheAdmittedSets` derives all four parser vocabularies (states, operations, effects, transports) from switch-case lists resolved through string consts, both directions plus size, and pins `conformanceOperations` to the derived operation set — the \\\"pinned by\\\" citation now holds. Refused samples restated as sampling bounds over the unbounded string domain and extended with the reviewer's exact survivor strings (`detached`, `detach`, `input_reopened`, `ssh_tunnel`), each now behaviorally refused.\\n- BOUNDS (recorded, not closed): W11 (DigestFile allowlist is function-wide, no detail pin), W13 (bespoke error types outside both spellings), mismatchf format-verb interpolation (derivation now fatals on any constructor call without exactly one string-literal argument — zero such sites today; vet catches non-constant formats). P11 stale bound dropped (C20 killed); P13 declined closure stands.\\n- TOOLING: round-3 runner (`.temp/TASK-260830-1snnef-r2/probe.py` family successor `.temp/TASK-260830-1snnef-r3/probe3.py`) snapshots and hash-verifies every touched file regardless of extension, with a JSON-restore self-test and a porcelain+fingerprint tree-identity check — a T01-shaped JSON mutation can no longer contaminate the tree.\\n- EVIDENCE: 21/21 replayed red, 0 survived, 0 anchor-missing (G1x6 incl. control, G2x5 incl. control and unused-var, G3x4 incl. init injection and both reclassifications, G4x5 incl. control, F2 guard). Tree verified identical before/after (porcelain + watched hashes).\\n- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/conformance_test.go` (G1/G3-comment/G4), `internal_pin_test.go` (G3 pin), `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (G2 twin + single-arg assertion + bounds), `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry + P11 correction). No production change, no arm-table change, 193/193 undisturbed.\\n- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14/14), `-race` on terminalbackend exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (`acceptance_cases=76`, `clauses_discharged=17/403`). Package coverage 90.0% statements. Rework left uncommitted in the working tree per the brief (board checkpoints, no commit).\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1snnef round-3 rework: unpinned legacyForward closed by a white-box pin, plus a correction\\n- CORRECTION: the round-1 and round-2 entries above claim C20 (`legacyForward` gains `\\\"screen\\\"`) is killed by `TestLegacyReverseProjectionExistsOnlyForThePair` and drop the P11 bound on that basis. That claim is false, and the error is the reviewer's (round-2 verdict), not the producer's — the rework followed the verdict. C20 lands on `BuiltinTmux` while `ProjectToLegacy` iterates a map, so the kill was a coin flip over iteration order: 5 red and 7 green across 12 runs of the reviewer's own probe. A single red on a map-iteration mutant proves nothing. LESSON, applied to every mutant below: a mutant over map iteration (or anything else iterating a map, e.g. `ProjectToLegacy`) is run repeatedly before its verdict is believed.\\n- FIX (H1, blocking): new white-box `TestLegacyForwardIsExactlyTheImmutablePair` (`internal_pin_test.go`) holds the live `legacyForward` map to exactly `{tmux, conpty}` in both directions plus the size — the `replicationMembers` idiom from this same CR — and additionally pins injectivity (distinct canonical values), which `ProjectToLegacy`'s documented determinism rested on unenforced. The black-box forward comment is restated to its half (sampling bound, not closure) with the reverse cited, and the reviewer's escape strings join the refused samples (`TranslateLegacyBackend(\\\"screen\\\")`, `ProjectToLegacy(\\\"vendor.screen\\\")`).\\n- FIX (H2, bound, closed cheaply): new `rejectPlainErrorAliases` fails the suite on any `errors.New`/`fmt.Errorf`-kin reference outside direct-call position, in every function including the two allowlisted ones (an alias inside `validatePlatforms` would bypass the funneled detail pin). Stated bounds and the allowlist test comment record the closure. Bespoke error types outside both spellings remain the disclosed bound.\\n- EVIDENCE: L3 (`\\\"screen\\\": \\\"vendor.screen\\\"`) 12/12 red, C20 (`\\\"screen\\\": BuiltinTmux`) 12/12 red, each over `-run TestLegacy|TestHistorical`; the new pin alone red on C20 with the size message (`holds 3 names, want exactly 2`); H2 alias (`var newPlain = errors.New` + call from a FuncDecl) 3/3 red on `TestPlainErrors`. Tree verified identical before/after (file-content compare + restore assert).\\n- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/internal_pin_test.go` (H1 pin), `conformance_test.go` (H1 comment + 2 samples), `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (H2 alias gate + bounds), `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry). No production change, no arm-table change, 193/193 undisturbed.\\n- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14/14), `-race` on terminalbackend exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (`acceptance_cases=76`, `clauses_discharged=17/403`). Rework left uncommitted in the working tree per the brief (board checkpoints, no commit).\\n\\n### 2321 — A local copy of a shared gate needs a pin, not a comment; a registry that only counts itself cannot see new code\\n- ROOT CAUSE (B3): `provhost.decodeStrictObject` re-implemented strict decoding without the shared `canonicaljson` surrogate rule, and Go's `encoding/json` replaces a lone `\\\\ud800` escape with U+FFFD silently — so Section 1.6 wire bodies carrying lone surrogates were admitted. Same class as the sibling story's decoder gap.\\n- FIX: local `hasLoneSurrogateEscape` gate in `internal/provhost/surrogate.go` (local copy because `canonicaljson` is frozen across both unlanded stories), called first from `decodeStrictObject`; one `\\\\ud800` fixture per production entry plus `TestSurrogateGateAgreesWithCanonicalJSON`, a 13-vector pin driving both the local gate and `canonicaljson.Canonicalize` so the copies cannot drift.\\n- ANOMALY: the first gate version used `switch` and reddened `TestAllProductionSwitchesAreClassified` — the package census bans switches as membership-gate hiding spots. Rewritten with if/else, identical verdicts, green. A gate's own residue rules apply to the fix too.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (B4): `tracecheck` verifies registry -> code only, so ~3,700 lines of `internal/provider` + `internal/provhost` landed with the gate green under gap prose asserting \\\"no provider manifest is implemented anywhere\\\". The census enumerates what registered itself.\\n- FIX: 4 acceptance cases + 4 section bindings (7.1, 7.6, 7.7, 8), 4 gap rewrites (5.5, 7.2, 7.3, 7.5), re-pinned hash; report now bindings=53 unevidenced=45 clauses 17/428. Reverse scan (every `internal/*` package owned or explicitly excluded) recorded as open work, not implemented here.\\n- DECISION (A2/A3/A4, recorded in code): CheckIdentity duplication is deliberate (different error surface, shared package frozen); Provider Protocol 3.0.0 is a stated non-owner bound, not a defect; provider's cause-appending errors must be rebuilt, not quoted, at the future cmd/ax lift (`refuseCausalLeak`).\\n- SCOPE: `internal/provhost/surrogate*.go`, `protocol.go`, refusal inventory (floor 162->164), `profile_test.go` (cross-plane set test), `identity.go`/`doc.go` bounds, `internal/provider/doc.go` composition contract, ownership registry + pin + report/golden/README figures.\\n- STATUS: Resolved. `go test ./...` and `-cover` green, vet + GOOS=windows vet + gofmt clean, admit-all and narrowing mutants red as required. TASK-260830-32jeti round-4, handed to review.\\n\\n### 1244 — A deadline borrowed from pipe ownership is not a deadline; a shared hand list is not a pin\\n- ROOT CAUSE (F1): the `os.Pipe` rewrite in `internal/provhost/runner.go` fixed the Wait-closes-StdoutPipe race but removed the only thing that unblocked the post-Wait drain. `exec.WaitDelay` closes pipes exec itself owns; with caller-supplied `*os.File` pipes nothing closes them, so `readCapped` waits for EOF until every writer is gone and a setsid-detached grandchild holds `Host.Call` open for its whole lifetime (measured 20.3-20.7s against sleep 20, frame accepted with err=nil).\\n- FIX: the waiter owns the bound now — `command.Wait()` runs in a goroutine under `select` on the call context, both drains collect through `collectDrains` under the same context, and closing the read ends fails blocked drains at once. A `Process.Kill` backstop covers a self-detached direct child, which the group-aimed `Cancel` misses. The round-6 EPIPE rule is untouched: with the wait reaped and stdout holding a frame, the frame still governs.\\n- ANOMALY: the first regression probe passed vacuously in 0.79s — python3 cold start under load can exceed the 400ms deadline kill, so no grandchild ever existed to hold the pipe. A hang test whose fixture loses a startup race proves nothing. Rebuilt on perl (millisecond start) with the kill seconds away; 3/3 red at the sleeper lifetime before the fix, green at the deadline after.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (F2): the 13-vector corpus was literal-versus-literal — both implementations matched the same hand list, so a narrowed low-surrogate ceiling (SG1, 1023 admitted) and a narrowed uppercase hex range (SG5, 473 admitted) survived 6/6. Raw WTF-8 (`\\\\xed\\\\xa0\\\\x80`) arrived through an encoding the escape scanner never sees and became U+FFFD silently.\\n- FIX: `decodeStrictObject` refuses non-UTF-8 first (mirroring `canonicaljson.decodeStrict` order), and the corpus is replaced by a 239,630-vector derived sweep — full BMP x hex case, surrogate x 16 case mixes, high x boundary/non-low seconds, sampled positions plus all-surrogate member names, full BMP raw (WTF-8 form for surrogates), malformed patterns, astral samples — every verdict judged by the independent implementation. SG1 diverges on 19,482 vectors, SG5 on 4,411; gate removal reddens the identity row with err=nil and the sweep on 2,059.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (F3): `checkResponseMembers` ran before the version gate, so only a v2-shaped 3.x envelope reached `incompatible_protocol`; the tree's own pinned 7.2 quote scopes that member rule to major 2. Fixed the ordering, not the doc: a `foreignMajor` peek (protocol identity plus readable foreign version, trusts nothing, refuses nothing) skips the v2 `ok`/member rules so the single existing mismatch site decides. No new refusal arm; floor untouched by F3.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/provhost/runner.go`, `protocol.go`, `surrogate*.go`, `identity.go` + comment corrections, `runner_test.go`, `protocol_test.go`, `identity_test.go`, refusal inventory (floor 164->166: one UTF-8 frame arm plus its status-body expansion, each witnessed).\\n- STATUS: Resolved. Build, vet, GOOS=windows vet, gofmt clean; `go test ./...` 15/15 green; provhost `-race` green; provhost 85.8%, provider 97.0%. TASK-260830-32jeti round-8, handed to review.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-32jeti: two green branches, one red combination — syscall.Mkfifo under GOOS=windows vet\\n- FINDING: the new CI step `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` failed on the merged tree with `terminalbackend_test.go:972:20: undefined: syscall.Mkfifo` — the only failure across all 16 packages. Invisible on both parents by construction: the story branch added the gate before the package existed (nothing to compile, exit 0), and trunk added the `syscall.Mkfifo` FIFO case without the gate (never compiled under Windows). Each branch was green on its own; only the combination is red. A per-branch gate that never meets the code it must check proves nothing about the merge.\\n- FIX: moved only the FIFO case out of `TestDigestFile` into `TestDigestFileRefusesFIFO` in new `internal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend_unix_test.go`, following the `internal/localstore/projection_unix_test.go` pattern. Correction worth recording: the `_unix` filename suffix alone constrains nothing (`unix` is a build tag, not a GOOS value, so the suffix form matches no `_GOOS` pattern) — the first attempt with suffix-only still failed windows vet, and the explicit `//go:build unix` line is what excludes Windows. The shared test file drops the `syscall` import and keeps a pointer comment; no other Go file touched.\\n- EVIDENCE: `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./... -count=1` 16/16 green with `TestDigestFileRefusesFIFO` observed PASS on linux (a moved test that stops executing is not a fix), `tracecheck` exit 0. TASK-260830-32jeti, handed to review.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0: sessadapter closed-vocabulary census derived from the pinned document, vocab gates looped, acceptance cases registered\\n- FIX: `census_test.go` used `specdoc` without deriving from it (vet failure on the unused import). Added `TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec` (20 closed bodies: every Required list in document order plus the Members map as a set, with the success/failure envelopes derived by the spec's own first-four-fields rule, the manifest from its table's first-column spans, and the doctor result from the operation table) and `TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec` (16 vocabularies pinned to their spec unions; operation/capability registries in order, value sets as sets).\\n- FINDINGS (all verified against the raw document, each would have been a silent wrong-source derivation): the request envelope sentence exists three times (7.5-style, 7.8, 7.9) and the capability-value sentence twice (Provider Probe 7.4 vs Session Adapter Probe 7.8) — selection is by a structural fragment only the Session Adapter sentence carries, and the parse still covers the whole sentence; member sentences contain digit-period-digit abbreviations (`Section 7.5`, `Structured Error 1.1`), so the sentence scanner skips those; unions use three pipe encodings (`\\\\|` in the operation table, raw `|` in prose, `&#124;` in the manifest table); the manifest table pairs members per row (`schema`/`schema_version` etc.), so the first cell contributes every bare snake_case span; the `probe` row name recurs in four tables, so row unions are windowed to the 7.8 registry table; fidelity profiles come from the `projection-plan` operation row (4 values — the 13.14 `Profiles are` sentence lists 5 including `archive_only`, which is a strategy there, never a profile).\\n- REFACTOR (production-first, same `var` + `validX` loop idiom the package already uses): `capabilityStatuses`/`validCapabilityStatus` (probe.go), `readPurposes`/`validReadPurpose` and `findingSeverities`/`validFindingSeverity` (context.go), `tupleArchitectures`/`validTupleArchitecture` (tuple.go); the four inline-literal checks now loop the tables. Roles, directions, candidate kinds, and platforms derive from the existing `Role`/`Direction`/`CandidateKind`/`scalar.Platform` consts with no production change (tuple platforms delegate to `scalar.ParsePlatform`).\\n- TEST: new `TestDecodeProbeClosedRules/bad_status` — no behavioral test refused a fifth status, so a `return true` mutant of `validCapabilityStatus` survived the suite with the static census green. The mutant is now killed by the entry point (`DecodeProbe`).\\n- EVIDENCE (executed mutants, `/tmp/sessadapter-mutants.sh`, tree verified identical before/after): M1 `capabilityStatuses`+`bogus` killed by `TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec`; M2 `findingSeverities`+`fatal` killed by `TestDecodeFindingRules/bad_severity`; M3 `requestMembers`+`zzz` killed by `TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec/request_envelope`; M4 `validCapabilityStatus`→`return true` (all searched-for tokens preserved) leaves the static census green and is killed by the behavioral suite (`TestDecodeProbeClosedRules/bad_status`); M5 unregistered vocabulary-shaped `var` killed by `TestClosedVocabularyTablesAreRegistered`. 8/8 as required, 0 survived.\\n- TRACEABILITY: 7 acceptance cases appended (`session-adapter-discovery/-manifest/-probe/-operations/-limits/-idempotency/-tuple-gates`, each bound to one production declaration and its named positive/refusal tests), digest re-pinned to `78d9bc9b...`, count pins 81->88, README ownership paragraph 81->88 plus a sessadapter disclosure paragraph that keeps the Section 7.8 clause-level binding `unevidenced` (no clause enumerated — no clause-level claim made).\\n- NOTE (pre-existing, not touched): README still says \\\"One admitted binding out of forty-nine\\\" while `tracecheck` measures `bindings=53` — stale since before this task (first run here already showed 53). Flagged for the review rather than fixed in passing.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/sessadapter/{census_test,probe,context,tuple}.go` + `probe_test.go` (bad status), `internal/traceability/{ownership.v0.5.0.json,traceability.go,traceability_test.go,cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go}`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry). Work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n=== git log worktree ===\\n=== status ===\\n M LOGBOOK.md\\n M README.md\\n M internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go\\n M internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json\\n M internal/traceability/traceability.go\\n M internal/traceability/traceability_test.go\\n?? internal/sessadapter/\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 20378,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 5095,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
