{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d025","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07476-3862-7671-a25f-75740245e24f"},"sequence":1645,"recorded_at":1780531400003285,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"2c321108-c95b-419c-b093-4145adb636d8"},"task_id":"2c321108-c95b-419c-b093-4145adb636d8","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"2c321108-c95b-419c-b093-4145adb636d8","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-40-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -n 30 LOGBOOK.md; echo \\\"...\\\"; grep -n \\\"TASK-260830-2z3se0\\\" LOGBOOK.md | head\",\n  \"description\": \"Check logbook format\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-06\\n\\n### 0515 — Session-adapter leaf round-3 rework: rev2 B1–B3 closed, N4/N5 closed-or-bounded\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2z3se0 round-3 rework (review-verdict-rev2, changes requested, B1–B3 blocking + N4/N5). All changes inside `internal/sessadapter/` except this entry. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (B1): `checkValidateResult` no longer calls `checkValidateNullability` — the pinned §7.8 validate success member list names no target members, so the request-body nullability rule cannot apply to successes. Archive-mode validate success now passes through `CheckSuccessBody`; `TestValidateSuccessAdmitsEveryMode` drives staged/live/archive successes. The round-2 anomaly below is resolved, not decided: the document's own success-body list settles it.\\n- FIX (B2): `TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec` now compares the Members gate map as a set against the derived list for all four tail bodies (success, failure, manifest, doctor); the `manifestMembers` local is renamed `derivedManifest` so it cannot shadow the production map; the log reports member-map comparisons (20 across 21 bodies; SupportedContractVersions has no production gate map by design).\\n- FIX (B3): new `TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction` derives the constructor denominator from production — every `axerror.New` site must sit inside a registered constructor body, and the registered set must equal the error-constructing vars exactly. The inventory header sentence now states what both gates do.\\n- FIX (N4): new `TestCheckCallBindingZeroFactsRefuse` — all five `CheckCallBinding` zero-fact exemptions refuse through their own arms.\\n- FIX (N5): `vocabularyTablesInFile` handles shared and paired multi-name initializers (synthetic vectors added); the tagless-switch exemption is confined to `readUTF16Escape` by function name (`classifySwitch` + `TestSwitchClassifierNamesItsExemption`); the census stated bound now names the function-local obligation lists (pinned behaviourally, both directions) and the const/regexp shapes (absent from production).\\n- EVIDENCE: narrowing-mutant battery over the rework scope, every mutant grep-confirmed present and compiling before its verdict; full gates green (see the attached rework-evidence note).\\n\\n### 0444 — Session-adapter leaf rework: all four blocking verdict findings closed, one anomaly reported\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2z3se0 round-2 rework (review-verdict-rev1, changes requested, F1–F4 blocking + F5–F7). All changes inside `internal/sessadapter/`; previously reviewed files untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (F1): nine inline closed unions → table loops with `valid*` consultants (mode, direction, entry status, registry-entry status, evidence result, candidate kind, role, context-free ops). Refusal details byte-identical, 323-arm inventory unchanged. Census scanner extended two ways: named slice/map types resolve package-wide; new `TestNoUnregisteredInlineVocabularies` forbids any chain comparing one operand against 2+ closed values. The new detector immediately found two more real unions (probe candidate kind, manifest/probe context dispatch) the reviewer had not listed. Spec pins for all eight unions; registrations 55 → 63.\\n- FIX (F2): `collectFileArms` exempts only the definition Name in its ValueSpec; `var x = ctor` fails package-level and function-local. `TestConstructorAliasSpellingsFailDerivation` replays all four probes on synthetic sources.\\n- FIX (F3): `TestSurrogatePairSweep` — every high × {lowLo−1, lowLo, lowHi, lowHi+1} plus full-range interior for three highs, verdicts from test-local literals: 2058 refused + 5124 admitted.\\n- FIX (F4): per-member drivers for doctor-required (4×2 writer variants), nullability (4×2 branches, request side), applicable checks (3) + nullable-bool types (3).\\n- FIX (F5/F6/F7): same-length echo forgery; exact/over frame edges on all three envelopes; four zero-value host-fact refusals.\\n- EVIDENCE: narrowing-mutant battery 26 killed + 1 control-green / 27 measured, every mutant grep-confirmed present and compiling before its verdict (`/tmp/mutant-battery.py`, log attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-battery-rev2.log`). Gates: `go test ./...` 17/17 exit 0, sessadapter 904 PASS/0 FAIL, `-count=3` green, `-race` green, cover 81.1% → 81.4%, vet + GOOS=windows vet exit 0, gofmt clean.\\n- ANOMALY (behavior preserved, needs product decision): `checkValidateNullability` is shared by request and success bodies, but validate success bodies carry no target members and the member set is exact, so archive-mode success ALWAYS refuses (`carries a target member` on absent members, reproduced with a scratch test) while staged/live success passes vacuously — the success-side call is a mode gate in disguise. F4 driven request-side where the rule is well-defined. Options: scope the rule to requests / redesign absent-handling / declare archive success impossible.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\\n## 2026-09-05\\n...\\n10:- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2z3se0 round-3 rework (review-verdict-rev2, changes requested, B1–B3 blocking + N4/N5). All changes inside `internal/sessadapter/` except this entry. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n20:- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2z3se0 round-2 rework (review-verdict-rev1, changes requested, F1–F4 blocking + F5–F7). All changes inside `internal/sessadapter/`; previously reviewed files untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n26:- EVIDENCE: narrowing-mutant battery 26 killed + 1 control-green / 27 measured, every mutant grep-confirmed present and compiling before its verdict (`/tmp/mutant-battery.py`, log attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-battery-rev2.log`). Gates: `go test ./...` 17/17 exit 0, sessadapter 904 PASS/0 FAIL, `-count=3` green, `-race` green, cover 81.1% → 81.4%, vet + GOOS=windows vet exit 0, gofmt clean.\\n925:### TASK-260830-2z3se0: sessadapter closed-vocabulary census derived from the pinned document, vocab gates looped, acceptance cases registered\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6142,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1536,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
