{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d06d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07476-3862-7671-a25f-75740245e24f"},"sequence":1681,"recorded_at":1780531400003357,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4727530c-d257-449f-9504-a7a1e57e582a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"ee9ee065-93f1-4c9f-923f-b5d20a75b3c1"},"task_id":"ee9ee065-93f1-4c9f-923f-b5d20a75b3c1","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"ee9ee065-93f1-4c9f-923f-b5d20a75b3c1","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-06\n-\n-### 0515 — Session-adapter leaf round-3 rework: rev2 B1–B3 closed, N4/N5 closed-or-bounded\n+## 2026-09-06\n+\n+### 0618 — Session-adapter leaf round-4 rework: rev3 B4/B5/B6 closed as classes, N6 fixed in code\n+\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2z3se0 round-4 rework (review-verdict-rev3, changes requested, B4–B6 blocking + N6). Test-only additions inside `internal/sessadapter/` (`zero_absent_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `import_census_test.go`) plus a two-line production-test fix in `inventory_test.go` and this entry. No production behavior change; the 323-arm inventory floor is untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\n+- FIX (B4): the zero/absent-fact class is now derived, not listed. `TestEnvelopeEchoEmptyStringRefuses` iterates the echo members from the production Required slices (request [:2], success/failure [:4] = 10 rows) with wants from `ProtocolID`/`ProtocolVersion`/`wantRequest()`, each driven as `\"\"` through its entry point; `TestCheckTargetWriteGatesAbsentAdapterRefuses` deletes each required adapter name (set derived from `DoctorRequiredCapabilities`) and both writers together; `TestCapabilityUsableAbsentIsNotUsable` deletes every `capabilityOrder` name through both `CapabilityUsable` and `capabilityMapUsable`; `TestCheckDoctorHealthyRefusesEmptyRequiredName` pins the name gate against `\"\"`.\n+- FIX (B5): `TestStringBoundEdges` (17 rows: all 16 survivor `checkStringBounds` maxima plus probe detail 0..2048) drives min-1/min/max/max+1 through the entry; `TestArrayBoundEdges` drives 0/1/max/max+1 for argv count, disposition lists, contract rows, and versions. Same-width sortable fixtures where the gate orders members (zero-padded `c01..c64` contract ids, `1.0.0-a01..a33` prerelease versions); the 8-entry disposition refusal lands on the count arm because it fires before the element gates.\n+- FIX (B6): new `TestAxerrorImportsAreUnaliased` — every production import of the error path must bind `axerror` (default or identical alias); renamed, blank, and dot bindings fail, with a zero-importer fail-closed guard. The constructor census is now sound as written without special-casing aliases. Synthetic alias vectors prove the gate shape.\n+- FIX (N6): `constructorSitesInFile` now reports the function-local registered-name case (`case !topLevel`, was a silent fall-through), matching its comment; pinned by synthetic `TestConstructorSitesReportFunctionLocalRegisteredName` (reports locally, stays exempt at package level).\n+- EVIDENCE: narrowing-mutant battery 36/36 killed, 0 survived — exactly the reviewer's 35 survivors (10 envelope + 3 presence + 20 bounds + 2 alias) plus the N6 arm. Every mutant grep-confirmed present and `go vet`-clean before its verdict; tree sha-verified identical after. A3/A4 additionally hold the constructor census green, so the kill comes from the import census, not the floor. Harness lesson: piped `go test | tail` reports tail's exit 0 — the first battery run showed 0/36 for that reason; all gate statuses here are unpiped direct exit codes.\n+- GATES: `go build ./...` 0, `go vet ./...` 0, `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./...` 17/17 exit 0 (sessadapter 976 PASS/0 FAIL, cover 81.5%), `-race` on sessadapter exit 0, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=88, unchanged — no behavior change, no new AC rows).\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\n+\n+### 0515 — Session-adapter leaf round-3 rework: rev2 B1–B3 closed, N4/N5 closed-or-bounded\n"}}}
